1
00:00:01,101 --> 00:00:04,338
[theme song playing]
<i>♪ In the not-too-distant future ♪</i>

2
00:00:04,404 --> 00:00:06,206
<i>♪ Next Sunday AD ♪</i>

3
00:00:07,508 --> 00:00:10,377
<i>♪ There was a guy named Joel ♪</i>

4
00:00:10,444 --> 00:00:12,880
<i>♪ Not too different from you or me ♪</i>

5
00:00:13,714 --> 00:00:16,617
<i>♪ He worked at Gizmonic Institute ♪</i>

6
00:00:16,717 --> 00:00:19,620
<i>♪ Just another face in a red jumpsuit ♪</i>

7
00:00:19,686 --> 00:00:22,623
<i>♪ He did a good job</i>
<i>Cleaning up the place ♪</i>

8
00:00:22,723 --> 00:00:24,458
<i>♪ But his bosses didn't like him ♪</i>

9
00:00:24,525 --> 00:00:26,493
<i>♪ So they shot him into space! ♪</i>

10
00:00:29,229 --> 00:00:32,366
<i>♪ We'll send him cheesy movies! ♪</i>

11
00:00:32,432 --> 00:00:34,601
<i>♪ The worst we can find! </i>♪

12
00:00:34,668 --> 00:00:35,502
<i>♪ La la la ♪</i>

13
00:00:35,569 --> 00:00:38,372
<i>♪ He'll have to sit and watch them all ♪</i>

14
00:00:38,472 --> 00:00:40,774
<i>♪ And we'll monitor his mind! </i>♪

15
00:00:40,841 --> 00:00:41,675
♪<i> La la la ♪</i>

16
00:00:41,742 --> 00:00:44,778
<i>♪ Now keep in mind Joel can't control ♪</i>

17
00:00:44,845 --> 00:00:47,014
<i>♪ Where the movies begin or end </i>♪

18
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:47,915
<i>♪ La la la ♪</i>

19
00:00:48,015 --> 00:00:50,984
<i>♪ Because he used those special parts ♪</i>

20
00:00:51,084 --> 00:00:54,154
<i>♪ To make his robot friends ♪</i>

21
00:00:55,989 --> 00:00:58,058
<i>-♪ Robot roll call </i>♪
-[man on radio]<i> Let's go. Cambot!</i>

22
00:00:58,125 --> 00:00:59,593
{\an8}-[man] Pan left.
-♪ Gypsy! ♪

23
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:01,028
{\an8}<i>-Hi, girl!</i>
-♪ Tom Servo! ♪

24
00:01:01,094 --> 00:01:02,029
{\an8}<i>What a cool guy.</i>

25
00:01:02,095 --> 00:01:03,597
{\an8}<i>-♪ Croooow! ♪</i>
-Wisecracker.

26
00:01:03,697 --> 00:01:06,633
<i>♪ If you're wondering</i>
<i>How he eats and breathes ♪</i>

27
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:08,669
<i>♪ And other science facts ♪</i>

28
00:01:08,735 --> 00:01:09,570
♪<i> La la la ♪</i>

29
00:01:09,636 --> 00:01:12,940
<i>♪ Then repeat to yourself</i>
<i>It's just a show ♪</i>

30
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:15,842
<i>♪ I should really just relax ♪</i>

31
00:01:15,943 --> 00:01:21,048
<i>♪ For Mystery Science Theater 3000! ♪</i>

32
00:01:31,758 --> 00:01:33,927
OK, Gypsy, it's your turn, roll.

33
00:01:33,994 --> 00:01:35,996
Come on, boxcars!

34
00:01:36,964 --> 00:01:39,099
OK, looks like...

35
00:01:39,166 --> 00:01:41,068
Oh, got a six, OK.

36
00:01:41,134 --> 00:01:46,039
-One, two, three, four, five, six.
-[Servo moaning]

37
00:01:46,106 --> 00:01:48,909
Well, with each pop,
my mind expands at an alarming rate.

38
00:01:48,976 --> 00:01:49,977
And I don't mind telling you

39
00:01:50,043 --> 00:01:52,379
it's a harsh jarring
comfortless experience.

40
00:01:52,446 --> 00:01:53,947
Oh, come on, quit your bellyaching.

41
00:01:54,014 --> 00:01:55,816
Hi, everybody,
welcome to the Satellite of Love.

42
00:01:55,882 --> 00:01:57,351
I'm Joel Robinson in the box

43
00:01:57,417 --> 00:01:59,653
and I have decided to turn old Tom Servo

44
00:01:59,720 --> 00:02:02,155
in that Milton Bradley game Kaboom.

45
00:02:02,222 --> 00:02:03,557
OK, come on.

46
00:02:04,591 --> 00:02:05,726
Oh, got an 8.

47
00:02:06,727 --> 00:02:07,794
Oh, that stings.

48
00:02:07,861 --> 00:02:08,695
And that's another thing.

49
00:02:08,762 --> 00:02:09,663
Why Kaboom?

50
00:02:09,730 --> 00:02:12,232
Guys, I feel more suited
to go to the head of the class

51
00:02:12,299 --> 00:02:14,368
or Stadium Checkers or even Kerplunk.

52
00:02:14,434 --> 00:02:15,969
Anything would be better than this.

53
00:02:16,036 --> 00:02:17,838
If it would make you feel any better,

54
00:02:17,904 --> 00:02:19,940
we could play hands down with you.

55
00:02:20,073 --> 00:02:23,310
Why, that's it!
Oh, great day, hands down.

56
00:02:23,377 --> 00:02:26,346
That's the slap happiest game ever
I would be playing.

57
00:02:26,413 --> 00:02:27,581
I thought we just get in a circle

58
00:02:27,648 --> 00:02:28,882
and hit you and snag on you
and crush you--

59
00:02:29,016 --> 00:02:30,784
He, guys, I could, uh, surv--

60
00:02:30,851 --> 00:02:32,452
I got to go survey
the electronics on the ship.

61
00:02:32,519 --> 00:02:35,989
Could we just forget about the game
and pop up Servo's head until it pops?

62
00:02:36,056 --> 00:02:38,358
-Yeah. That's it.
-[Servo] No, no, no...

63
00:02:38,425 --> 00:02:42,562
-Pop him, pop him, pop, pop, pop.
-No, no. Please, please, please...

64
00:02:42,863 --> 00:02:46,433
[all except Servo]
Pop him, pop him, pop, pop, pop.

65
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:49,302
-Pop him, pop him, pop, pop, pop.
-[Servo whimpering]

66
00:02:49,369 --> 00:02:51,872
-Pop him, pop him, pop, pop, pop.
-No...

67
00:02:51,938 --> 00:02:54,107
-Pop him, pop him, pop, pop, pop.
-No...

68
00:02:56,543 --> 00:02:59,546
My Lord, this is incredible.
My head is so huge.

69
00:02:59,613 --> 00:03:01,148
I've accumulated all the knowledge

70
00:03:01,214 --> 00:03:03,417
of all humanity throughout the ages.

71
00:03:03,483 --> 00:03:05,786
Yet all I can think about is why,

72
00:03:05,852 --> 00:03:09,289
why did they cancel<i> Manimal, </i>why?

73
00:03:09,356 --> 00:03:13,393
Oh, uh, Pearl and Hayes
and Mary Healey are calling you guys.

74
00:03:14,728 --> 00:03:15,962
Oh, hello, Booby.

75
00:03:16,029 --> 00:03:18,532
Say, if you want to make
people's heads explode?

76
00:03:18,598 --> 00:03:19,966
Sure we all do.

77
00:03:20,267 --> 00:03:22,469
Well, my invention exchange this week

78
00:03:22,536 --> 00:03:25,939
is a study guide I've put together
called "The Scanner Planner."

79
00:03:26,239 --> 00:03:29,109
It's filled with lots
of life's little instructions

80
00:03:29,176 --> 00:03:32,879
on how you can scan people's brains
and make their heads explode.

81
00:03:33,213 --> 00:03:35,582
Now, the first thing
you'll need for your scanning

82
00:03:35,649 --> 00:03:36,883
is a good subject,

83
00:03:36,950 --> 00:03:40,554
someone who's your moral
and intellectual inferior.

84
00:03:40,854 --> 00:03:42,522
I wonder who that could be.

85
00:03:42,589 --> 00:03:44,791
Hi, Dr. Forrester, what you doing?

86
00:03:51,131 --> 00:03:53,533
Hey, you were scanning me, weren't you?

87
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:57,003
You tried to make my head explode,
you freaked out maniac.

88
00:03:57,070 --> 00:03:59,406
[Forrester groans in pain]

89
00:03:59,473 --> 00:04:01,808
This could take a while, Joel.
Back up to you.

90
00:04:03,477 --> 00:04:05,212
Sirs, when are you going to realize

91
00:04:05,278 --> 00:04:08,615
that when you kill each other,
you're only hurting yourselves.

92
00:04:08,682 --> 00:04:12,586
Anyway, our invention exchange
is based on one of the century's safest,

93
00:04:12,652 --> 00:04:15,756
softest and funniest concept:
the wiffle ball.

94
00:04:15,822 --> 00:04:17,457
Ha ha, It's fun.

95
00:04:17,524 --> 00:04:19,359
And we've taken the whole wiffle concept

96
00:04:19,426 --> 00:04:22,763
and siphoned it through our own
madcap irreverent viewpoint.

97
00:04:22,829 --> 00:04:25,899
For instance, there's the wiffle hat.

98
00:04:25,966 --> 00:04:29,603
It's lighter, cooler and more comfortable
than any ordinary hat.

99
00:04:29,669 --> 00:04:32,139
-And there's the wiffle glass.
-Oh, yeah.

100
00:04:32,205 --> 00:04:35,342
-Makes any soft drink wifflacious.
-Whoo...

101
00:04:35,408 --> 00:04:37,744
Well, we haven't quite
worked out all the kinks yet

102
00:04:37,811 --> 00:04:39,880
but I've come up
with something even cooler:

103
00:04:39,946 --> 00:04:41,448
wiffle cheese.

104
00:04:41,548 --> 00:04:43,950
Hey, wait a minute,
this is just Swiss cheese.

105
00:04:44,050 --> 00:04:46,219
That's right. It's nature's own wiffle.

106
00:04:46,286 --> 00:04:47,621
That's right. And think
of the possibilities,

107
00:04:47,687 --> 00:04:48,688
they're endless.

108
00:04:48,755 --> 00:04:52,025
Wiffle cat, wiffle dog,
wiffle roach motel.

109
00:04:52,092 --> 00:04:54,828
Wiffle sports jacket,
wiffle replacement hip,

110
00:04:54,895 --> 00:04:55,896
wiffle underpants.

111
00:04:55,962 --> 00:04:58,131
Wiffle shoehorn,
wiffle apartment building,

112
00:04:58,198 --> 00:04:59,599
wiffle Claude Akins.

113
00:04:59,666 --> 00:05:00,734
[together] Wiffle.

114
00:05:00,801 --> 00:05:02,035
What do you think, sirs?

115
00:05:06,239 --> 00:05:09,776
Oh, Joel, your movie this week
is your first western.

116
00:05:09,843 --> 00:05:11,111
It's called<i> Gunslinger</i>

117
00:05:11,178 --> 00:05:14,514
and it stars Beverly Garland
in her pre-Doddy period.

118
00:05:14,581 --> 00:05:16,483
Beverly Garland?
[rolls tongue]

119
00:05:18,051 --> 00:05:19,920
It's also directed by Roger Corman.

120
00:05:19,986 --> 00:05:22,889
So your heads may explode
before Frank's does.

121
00:05:22,956 --> 00:05:25,091
Yippiekiyay, mama jama.

122
00:05:30,297 --> 00:05:32,899
He made my head explode.
Thank you, Dr. Forrester.

123
00:05:32,966 --> 00:05:34,835
-[buzzer sounding]
-[all clamoring]

124
00:05:34,901 --> 00:05:36,069
[Servo] Thank you.

125
00:05:44,778 --> 00:05:46,580
[Crow] Ah, that feels good.

126
00:05:47,047 --> 00:05:50,317
[rooster crowing]

127
00:05:50,383 --> 00:05:52,419
[Crow] It's morning in America.

128
00:05:52,485 --> 00:05:53,787
[Servo] Let's see. Doctor? No.

129
00:05:53,854 --> 00:05:55,856
No barber? No, that's no good.

130
00:05:56,923 --> 00:05:59,693
Oh, law enforcement!
That's what I need.

131
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:01,828
[Joel] Now, to the horses.

132
00:06:01,895 --> 00:06:03,430
[Crow laughs] Corman.

133
00:06:04,264 --> 00:06:06,566
[Servo] She is slick.
How'd she slip by us?

134
00:06:10,370 --> 00:06:11,805
-Hi.
-Hi.

135
00:06:11,872 --> 00:06:13,540
-[Servo] You didn't hear her?
Some sheriff.

136
00:06:13,607 --> 00:06:14,975
Long night.

137
00:06:15,041 --> 00:06:16,176
Quiet one, for a change.

138
00:06:16,243 --> 00:06:17,711
[Crow] Any trouble with Patty, Marshall?

139
00:06:17,777 --> 00:06:18,945
Oh, you shouldn't get up so early

140
00:06:19,012 --> 00:06:20,881
just to fetch my breakfast.

141
00:06:20,947 --> 00:06:22,849
What else is a marshal's wife good for?

142
00:06:22,916 --> 00:06:25,719
[Servo] Formfitting Western dress,
nice bustier.

143
00:06:25,785 --> 00:06:27,187
So, what have you been doing all night?

144
00:06:27,254 --> 00:06:29,623
-[Joel] Cleaning my gun, yeah.
-...Nate Signo.

145
00:06:29,689 --> 00:06:31,725
You still think he shot Uriah Baker?

146
00:06:31,791 --> 00:06:32,859
I'm sure of it.

147
00:06:32,959 --> 00:06:34,327
[dog barking]

148
00:06:34,394 --> 00:06:36,029
[Crow] They're not that good
at sneaking up.

149
00:06:36,096 --> 00:06:37,297
[Servo] Well, sneaking up
had just been invented, so...

150
00:06:37,364 --> 00:06:39,599
I went over to Erica Page's yesterday.

151
00:06:39,666 --> 00:06:41,801
Time I got there, he was gone.

152
00:06:42,302 --> 00:06:44,838
I don't know.
Maybe she warned him I was coming.

153
00:06:44,905 --> 00:06:47,607
Anyway, I tracked him out
as far as Nine Mile Canyon,

154
00:06:47,674 --> 00:06:48,942
-then I lost him.
-[Crow] Copper tubing!

155
00:06:49,709 --> 00:06:51,645
Probably holed in there
somewhere now.

156
00:06:51,745 --> 00:06:54,814
You figure out what you're going to do
about Erica's tramps at the Red Dog?

157
00:06:54,915 --> 00:06:57,617
Now, who in the world
could stand up to that woman?

158
00:06:57,684 --> 00:06:59,719
-Try me.
-[Servo] You like me.

159
00:07:00,553 --> 00:07:03,023
Aw, you stick to making coffee, Rose.

160
00:07:03,089 --> 00:07:04,557
I'll take care of the criminal element.

161
00:07:04,624 --> 00:07:05,458
[gunshot]

162
00:07:05,525 --> 00:07:06,393
[Servo] Guess I won't.

163
00:07:08,228 --> 00:07:09,729
[Crow] More, more, more.

164
00:07:09,930 --> 00:07:10,864
[horse whinnies]

165
00:07:10,964 --> 00:07:13,066
[Joel] Oop, see you, Dave.
Gotta go get a haircut.

166
00:07:14,868 --> 00:07:16,803
[Servo] You see, this is before
barber poles moved.

167
00:07:16,870 --> 00:07:18,471
They just sat outside
and cranked 'em.

168
00:07:22,542 --> 00:07:23,476
[Crow] What a day!

169
00:07:23,543 --> 00:07:25,979
Well, better check the scones.

170
00:07:26,046 --> 00:07:28,348
[Joel] Oh, how am I going
to explain this to--

171
00:07:28,415 --> 00:07:30,083
Oh, that's right.

172
00:07:36,623 --> 00:07:39,359
[Servo] Hon, morning.
What'd you dream about last night?

173
00:07:39,426 --> 00:07:40,994
Let me think, let me think.

174
00:07:41,861 --> 00:07:43,463
[Crow] Well, at least, check his pulse.

175
00:07:43,530 --> 00:07:44,397
[Joel] Yeah.

176
00:07:45,098 --> 00:07:46,633
[Servo] Oh, poop.

177
00:07:49,102 --> 00:07:50,704
[Joel] The man with a golden arm.

178
00:07:50,770 --> 00:07:51,905
-[♪♪♪]
-[Joel] Walking this.

179
00:07:51,972 --> 00:07:53,807
[Crow] So, Corman did Swamp
Diamonds on Monday

180
00:07:53,873 --> 00:07:54,908
and this one on Wednesday.

181
00:07:54,975 --> 00:07:55,842
[Joel] Yep.

182
00:07:57,811 --> 00:07:59,312
[Joel] Origami in your live type.

183
00:07:59,379 --> 00:08:00,580
[Servo imitating trumpet]

184
00:08:01,348 --> 00:08:02,449
[all scream]

185
00:08:02,749 --> 00:08:04,384
[Servo cries] Hold me!

186
00:08:07,187 --> 00:08:09,522
[Joel] Looks like Bella Abzug.

187
00:08:09,823 --> 00:08:13,226
[Crow] My set is melting, melting.

188
00:08:14,761 --> 00:08:15,895
[Servo] Oh,<i> Spy vs. Spy </i>.

189
00:08:15,962 --> 00:08:18,431
[Joel] Uh, Zorro kind of, sort of...

190
00:08:26,406 --> 00:08:27,474
[Crow] You got me.

191
00:08:30,210 --> 00:08:31,978
[Servo] They got a choreographer,
that's a good sign.

192
00:08:34,914 --> 00:08:36,616
[Crow in old voice]
The old Fred West.

193
00:08:41,054 --> 00:08:44,391
[Joel] Ah, kids, don't change
a light bulb without supervision.

194
00:08:45,425 --> 00:08:46,559
[Servo] Oh, it's like<i> High Plains Drifter,</i>

195
00:08:46,626 --> 00:08:47,727
what with the red buildings and such.

196
00:08:47,794 --> 00:08:50,130
[Joel] No, it's<i> The Funny Company,</i>
as you can plainly see.

197
00:08:50,196 --> 00:08:51,364
[Servo makes buzzer sound]

198
00:08:54,501 --> 00:08:55,468
[Servo] Hey, garden.

199
00:08:57,537 --> 00:08:58,905
What's the news from the East?

200
00:08:58,972 --> 00:09:00,507
Well, the railroad's still in Waco.

201
00:09:00,573 --> 00:09:02,475
[Crow] The Harkawis are mad.
They want their money.

202
00:09:02,542 --> 00:09:03,843
...that new track for two weeks yet.

203
00:09:03,910 --> 00:09:05,545
We're all waitin' for that big letter.

204
00:09:05,612 --> 00:09:07,213
Yeah, and I'm waitin' to carry it.

205
00:09:07,280 --> 00:09:10,216
[Joel] Small talk of the Old West.

206
00:09:10,283 --> 00:09:11,317
[Servo] The Pony Express,

207
00:09:11,384 --> 00:09:13,119
when it absolutely positively
has to be there

208
00:09:13,186 --> 00:09:14,954
in three or four months or so.

209
00:09:15,021 --> 00:09:17,190
[Joel] Oh, yeah, sure,
I'll deliver your plans

210
00:09:17,257 --> 00:09:18,324
through the telegraph.

211
00:09:18,391 --> 00:09:19,859
You bet.

212
00:09:25,131 --> 00:09:27,067
[Crow] I think he moved. Kidding.

213
00:09:27,167 --> 00:09:28,535
Good folks of Oracle...

214
00:09:28,601 --> 00:09:30,570
-[Joel] Yeah.
-[Crow] Yes, that's me.

215
00:09:30,637 --> 00:09:34,274
...we are gathered here
to plant the last remains of Scott Hood...

216
00:09:34,340 --> 00:09:35,642
[Servo] Brother of boys in need.

217
00:09:35,708 --> 00:09:38,478
...gallant marshal of our fair community.

218
00:09:38,545 --> 00:09:40,313
[Joel] Goodness, he eulogizes well.

219
00:09:40,380 --> 00:09:42,782
Not since the Battle of Shiloh,

220
00:09:42,849 --> 00:09:46,186
when we showed them Yankees
what Confederate currency really meant...

221
00:09:46,252 --> 00:09:48,088
[Crow] He's got something there,
food for thought.

222
00:09:48,154 --> 00:09:50,056
...have I seen such bravery in one man.

223
00:09:51,224 --> 00:09:53,359
[Servo] Sorry, I'm late,
horse threw a tire.

224
00:09:53,426 --> 00:09:55,562
Oh! What are you doing here?

225
00:09:55,628 --> 00:09:57,297
Maybe he wanted to see
the results of his handiwork.

226
00:09:57,363 --> 00:09:58,364
[Joel] Ah, jeez, Jake.

227
00:09:58,431 --> 00:10:03,369
Well, the good work of Marshal Hood
has been terminated...

228
00:10:03,436 --> 00:10:05,405
near the hour of his triumph.

229
00:10:05,972 --> 00:10:07,073
[Servo snoring loudly]

230
00:10:07,140 --> 00:10:08,608
I'm sure you'll all be relieved to know

231
00:10:08,675 --> 00:10:12,345
-that I, acting in my capacity as mayor...
-[Servo whispers] Hey. Psst.

232
00:10:12,412 --> 00:10:15,482
have sent to San Antonio
for the celebrated Sam Bass.

233
00:10:15,548 --> 00:10:18,084
-[Joel] Big fish face guy.
-He's gonna be our new marshal.

234
00:10:19,786 --> 00:10:21,554
Well, so much for secular doings.

235
00:10:21,621 --> 00:10:23,256
[Servo] Let's party.

236
00:10:23,323 --> 00:10:24,657
Now, after I get through
sayin' the prayer,

237
00:10:24,724 --> 00:10:27,660
the good widow Hood will toss the first

238
00:10:27,727 --> 00:10:30,063
spade full of dirt
onto that old pine box there.

239
00:10:30,130 --> 00:10:32,065
[Joel] And then, she'll be singing
"Sunrise, Sunset."

240
00:10:32,132 --> 00:10:33,333
If you'll all kindly bend your necks.

241
00:10:33,399 --> 00:10:35,201
[Crow] And no goofing around
this time.

242
00:10:35,301 --> 00:10:36,402
[Servo] Can't bend my neck.

243
00:10:36,503 --> 00:10:37,804
Oh, Lord of man and beast...

244
00:10:37,871 --> 00:10:39,572
[Joel] Oh, now what?

245
00:10:39,639 --> 00:10:41,574
-...we poor sinners here...
-[Servo] Hey.

246
00:10:41,641 --> 00:10:43,276
...commit the lowly clay

247
00:10:43,343 --> 00:10:45,378
of your poor servant, Scott Hood...

248
00:10:45,445 --> 00:10:46,746
[Crow] Oh, knock it off, Herald.

249
00:10:46,813 --> 00:10:48,815
...to his last resting place

250
00:10:48,915 --> 00:10:52,986
here on Oracle's aspiring Boot Hill,

251
00:10:53,052 --> 00:10:56,256
until that mighty blast of Gabriel's horn

252
00:10:56,322 --> 00:10:58,191
on the final day of judgment.

253
00:10:58,258 --> 00:10:59,592
[Crow] I'm just winging it here, Lord.

254
00:10:59,659 --> 00:11:02,028
-Scott Hood...
-[Crow] What? I'm dead.

255
00:11:02,095 --> 00:11:03,296
...rest in peace.

256
00:11:04,564 --> 00:11:05,465
Amen.

257
00:11:05,565 --> 00:11:06,666
[Joel] Amen.

258
00:11:07,967 --> 00:11:09,068
[Servo] Hey, mine.

259
00:11:11,604 --> 00:11:13,406
[Joel] All right, I'm not doing
this one for free.

260
00:11:13,473 --> 00:11:14,440
Who was it, dear?

261
00:11:15,341 --> 00:11:17,310
One of the killers who went
after Scott last night.

262
00:11:17,377 --> 00:11:19,946
-[Crow] I'll just put this back.
-Then I guess that's all of them, huh?

263
00:11:20,013 --> 00:11:21,114
Not quite.

264
00:11:21,848 --> 00:11:23,783
I still have to settle
with whoever hired them.

265
00:11:24,217 --> 00:11:25,451
[Joel] Hey, I might not be dead
down here.

266
00:11:25,518 --> 00:11:27,320
You think it might be
somebody unknown behind this killin'?

267
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:29,055
There has to be, Mayor.

268
00:11:29,122 --> 00:11:31,591
Those men would have
no personal reason to do Scott in.

269
00:11:31,658 --> 00:11:33,393
Well, like I say,
Sam Bass'll be getting' here

270
00:11:33,459 --> 00:11:34,360
in a couple of weeks

271
00:11:34,427 --> 00:11:36,629
and he can take care of anything
that has to be taken care of.

272
00:11:36,729 --> 00:11:38,965
-He can be too late.
-Well...

273
00:11:39,032 --> 00:11:40,400
[Servo] Hey, I said, "I'm not dead."

274
00:11:40,466 --> 00:11:42,802
...Joshua's Deputy.
Want me to make him Marshal?

275
00:11:43,736 --> 00:11:45,271
[Joel] Well, it's so sudden.

276
00:11:45,338 --> 00:11:46,306
Not me, Mayor Polk.

277
00:11:46,372 --> 00:11:48,141
That kind of job takes book learnin'.

278
00:11:48,208 --> 00:11:49,442
[Crow] And some
basic intelligence.

279
00:11:49,509 --> 00:11:51,611
Is there a man here who thinks
he can handle the job?

280
00:11:51,978 --> 00:11:54,147
How 'bout me? I'd like to be marshal.

281
00:11:54,214 --> 00:11:55,481
Oh, shut up, little man.

282
00:11:55,548 --> 00:11:56,749
[Servo] You've got mending to do.

283
00:11:56,816 --> 00:11:58,484
Jake Hayes doesn't count.

284
00:11:58,551 --> 00:12:00,119
[Joel] But Sam Bass
is coming to town.

285
00:12:04,123 --> 00:12:06,693
[Joel] Would you want to go
have coffee sometime?

286
00:12:08,027 --> 00:12:08,962
Pin it on.

287
00:12:09,028 --> 00:12:10,296
[Servo] ♪ Pin it on
In the morning now ♪

288
00:12:10,363 --> 00:12:11,397
Pin it on who?

289
00:12:12,398 --> 00:12:13,666
On me.

290
00:12:13,733 --> 00:12:16,502
Oh, come on, Rose.
You must be pullin' my leg.

291
00:12:17,003 --> 00:12:18,771
I think it's a wonderful idea.

292
00:12:18,838 --> 00:12:20,640
-[Crow] What the...? Hey!
-With a woman marshal,

293
00:12:20,707 --> 00:12:23,509
Oracle'll be the hit
of the Western dime novels,

294
00:12:23,576 --> 00:12:25,979
and what bad man would
dream of shooting a woman?

295
00:12:26,045 --> 00:12:27,380
[Servo] Heh, I would.

296
00:12:27,981 --> 00:12:29,382
Pin it on.

297
00:12:29,449 --> 00:12:30,950
I can't do that.

298
00:12:31,050 --> 00:12:32,752
Oh, pin it on and get it over with.

299
00:12:32,819 --> 00:12:34,454
I've got a beef roast in the oven.

300
00:12:34,520 --> 00:12:37,156
[Crow] You know,
beef roast in the oven.

301
00:12:38,658 --> 00:12:40,893
-All right.
-[Joel] Well, I'm not very good at this,

302
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:43,529
usually I can't even put
a corsage on but...

303
00:12:45,031 --> 00:12:46,299
[Servo] Dink... ouch!

304
00:12:48,935 --> 00:12:51,437
[Crow] Now, to slip into
something sheriffy and sexy.

305
00:12:51,504 --> 00:12:54,207
[Joel] Well, back to the fellowship
hall for bars and punch.

306
00:12:54,274 --> 00:12:56,175
[Crow] Shouldn't they have
their headlights on?

307
00:12:58,678 --> 00:13:00,513
It's been a sad day, Mrs. Hood.

308
00:13:00,580 --> 00:13:03,883
This is the first chance I've had
to offer my personal condolences.

309
00:13:03,950 --> 00:13:05,451
Thank you, Erica.

310
00:13:05,518 --> 00:13:08,288
You've taken on a man's
responsibility, my dear.

311
00:13:08,388 --> 00:13:10,790
-I have Joshua here to help me.
-[Servo] The friend.

312
00:13:10,857 --> 00:13:13,393
Well, if there's anything
I can do, just let me know.

313
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:15,261
As a matter of fact, there is.

314
00:13:15,328 --> 00:13:17,297
[Crow] Can I borrow
that pink taffeta dress?

315
00:13:17,363 --> 00:13:19,065
There's a little matter
my husband kept putting off.

316
00:13:19,132 --> 00:13:20,233
[Servo] Me.

317
00:13:20,300 --> 00:13:21,934
I hate to mention it now, but I...

318
00:13:22,001 --> 00:13:24,070
I noticed you were open
past three this morning.

319
00:13:24,170 --> 00:13:27,040
The Red Dog Saloon is open 24 hours.

320
00:13:27,106 --> 00:13:28,641
-[Joel] Breakfast anytime.
-It has been.

321
00:13:29,208 --> 00:13:31,144
There's--there's
a curfew law, you know.

322
00:13:31,911 --> 00:13:34,213
I think you're taking
that star a bit too seriously.

323
00:13:34,781 --> 00:13:35,948
[Erica] Quite seriously.

324
00:13:36,015 --> 00:13:37,016
[Servo imitating gunshots]

325
00:13:37,083 --> 00:13:38,184
You're priceless.

326
00:13:39,285 --> 00:13:41,187
Drop in at my place tonight
for a free drink.

327
00:13:41,254 --> 00:13:42,455
[Servo] And keep the glass.

328
00:13:42,522 --> 00:13:43,723
Make it after three.

329
00:13:44,190 --> 00:13:46,826
-I'll be there.
-[Joel] Well, I have my men's group.

330
00:13:47,727 --> 00:13:49,562
I don't know,
I reckon some people

331
00:13:49,629 --> 00:13:51,130
won't think it's proper for a new widow

332
00:13:51,197 --> 00:13:53,933
to go around in pants
even though they are black.

333
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,802
Did you ever see
a peace officer in a corset?

334
00:13:55,868 --> 00:13:56,803
[Crow] Yeah, your husband.

335
00:13:56,869 --> 00:13:59,505
Lady, are you going
to wear that cannon?

336
00:13:59,572 --> 00:14:03,176
I don't imagine a bank robber
will change the rules just for me.

337
00:14:03,242 --> 00:14:05,511
Come on, Joshua,
let's start enforcing the law.

338
00:14:05,578 --> 00:14:07,313
[Servo] Close up for us, grumpy.

339
00:14:07,380 --> 00:14:08,781
[Joel] Oh, leather toilet seat cover.

340
00:14:10,450 --> 00:14:12,652
[lively piano music playing]

341
00:14:13,953 --> 00:14:16,422
-[Joel] Kind of looks like a ground round.
-[Servo] It does.

342
00:14:17,724 --> 00:14:20,226
-[Joel] Whee...
-[Servo] And there's my hinder.

343
00:14:23,596 --> 00:14:25,398
[Joel] You know, it's just possible
that's Rachmaninoff

344
00:14:25,465 --> 00:14:26,532
on the piano.

345
00:14:28,968 --> 00:14:30,870
[Crow] Hey, get off my ravioli.

346
00:14:33,973 --> 00:14:34,974
[Joel] Too good tonight.

347
00:14:35,041 --> 00:14:36,175
[Joel burps]

348
00:14:37,510 --> 00:14:40,646
[Servo] Oh, it's so hot in here,
we're so sassy.

349
00:14:43,282 --> 00:14:46,185
[Servo] Oh, we did not mean
to do that but we did it.

350
00:14:50,056 --> 00:14:51,591
Well, sir, there we was

351
00:14:51,657 --> 00:14:53,559
in the swamps below Fort Donaldson.

352
00:14:53,626 --> 00:14:55,027
[Servo] Wearing skirts like them.

353
00:14:56,329 --> 00:14:58,297
Buckney said we had to surrender.

354
00:14:58,364 --> 00:15:00,400
[Crow] Oh, don't start.

355
00:15:00,466 --> 00:15:03,002
Never. I went with Bedford Forrest.

356
00:15:03,069 --> 00:15:04,704
[Joel] You never knew
Bedford Forrest.

357
00:15:04,771 --> 00:15:05,805
...did at night,

358
00:15:05,872 --> 00:15:08,641
us ridin' piggyback with Forrest troopers.

359
00:15:09,475 --> 00:15:12,278
Next day, 10,000 surrendered,

360
00:15:12,345 --> 00:15:14,514
but me and Bedford
went out to fight another day.

361
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:15,948
[Servo] Well, go fish.

362
00:15:16,015 --> 00:15:17,250
[♪♪♪]

363
00:15:17,316 --> 00:15:19,285
[Crow] They kind of
look like bodybuilders.

364
00:15:19,986 --> 00:15:21,554
[Servo] Their underwear
has Raiders logos.

365
00:15:23,389 --> 00:15:25,691
[Joel] OK, go wash up, girls.

366
00:15:25,758 --> 00:15:28,694
[applause]

367
00:15:28,761 --> 00:15:31,030
[Crow] Excuse me,
I've got to go fire them.

368
00:15:32,465 --> 00:15:33,966
Is it three yet?

369
00:15:34,033 --> 00:15:35,501
-[Servo] Where's the headliner?
-Yes.

370
00:15:36,335 --> 00:15:37,770
She won't show her face.

371
00:15:37,837 --> 00:15:40,139
[Crow] Doodly, doodly, doodly,
dooie, her face.

372
00:15:42,241 --> 00:15:43,576
Good evening, Rose.

373
00:15:43,676 --> 00:15:44,777
Good morning, Erica.

374
00:15:45,244 --> 00:15:46,546
Did you come for that drink?

375
00:15:46,612 --> 00:15:47,713
I'll have a Sex on the Beach.

376
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:50,917
I'm afraid I don't have time for one.
It's after three, you know.

377
00:15:50,983 --> 00:15:52,618
Oh, now, Mrs. Hood...

378
00:15:53,119 --> 00:15:55,588
The Red Dog is open 24 hours.

379
00:15:55,655 --> 00:15:56,856
-Mm-hmm.
-[Crow] Breakfast anytime.

380
00:15:56,923 --> 00:15:58,825
Well, you well, you empty
your house and put out the lights.

381
00:15:59,759 --> 00:16:01,160
Put 'em out yourself.

382
00:16:04,330 --> 00:16:06,499
[Joel] Whoa, it's like
a lady<i> Road House.</i>

383
00:16:07,266 --> 00:16:08,468
[Servo] Samuel Beckett there.

384
00:16:10,236 --> 00:16:12,472
[Crow] At the second show,
dry mud wrestling.

385
00:16:13,406 --> 00:16:15,408
[Servo] Ooh, Beverly's wearing jackboots.

386
00:16:17,910 --> 00:16:19,679
[Crow] I'm a grim, old warrior.

387
00:16:19,779 --> 00:16:22,281
[clattering]

388
00:16:26,853 --> 00:16:28,020
[Servo] No, Joel, say what you will,

389
00:16:28,087 --> 00:16:29,956
but Roger Corman pushes my buttons.

390
00:16:31,424 --> 00:16:32,492
[grunting]

391
00:16:34,093 --> 00:16:36,162
[Servo] Well, that thing's not
helping any. Come here.

392
00:16:42,535 --> 00:16:44,403
[Crow] You want a fresh lime, Wormy?

393
00:16:44,470 --> 00:16:47,840
[Joel] You know, he should have slid
him across the bars probably.

394
00:16:47,907 --> 00:16:48,908
[Servo] Well, they hadn't
invented that yet.

395
00:16:48,975 --> 00:16:52,478
All right, everybody
who can walk, up and out.

396
00:16:52,545 --> 00:16:53,880
This place is closed for the night.

397
00:16:53,946 --> 00:16:55,882
[Joel] Hey, it's Jesse White
and Bob Crane,

398
00:16:55,982 --> 00:16:57,483
-I don't believe it.
-[Servo] Oh.

399
00:16:57,550 --> 00:17:00,086
[Crow] Hey, but this place
is open 24 hours.

400
00:17:01,153 --> 00:17:03,022
[Servo] They're taking
the elevator up apparently.

401
00:17:06,292 --> 00:17:08,494
You sure made a sick chicken
out of Erica Page.

402
00:17:08,561 --> 00:17:09,462
[Servo clucking]

403
00:17:09,529 --> 00:17:10,463
She's gonna be a sicker chicken

404
00:17:10,530 --> 00:17:12,231
when I find out what she has
to do with Nate Signo.

405
00:17:12,298 --> 00:17:13,900
[Crow] Hey, can I get
a new bucket in here?

406
00:17:13,966 --> 00:17:16,035
Well, you better get
some sleep, Miss Rose.

407
00:17:16,736 --> 00:17:18,504
Yeah, I guess I'd better.

408
00:17:19,305 --> 00:17:20,673
I'll--I'll curl up in there

409
00:17:20,740 --> 00:17:22,942
and then I'll spell ya'
in a couple of hours.

410
00:17:24,277 --> 00:17:27,013
[Joel] And you don't mind
if I watch you sleep, do you?

411
00:17:29,482 --> 00:17:31,751
[Crow] Yeah, stew's really good here.

412
00:17:31,817 --> 00:17:34,253
Now look, you turn around
or I'll book you for rustling.

413
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:36,556
[Servo with drunk voice] I'm already
serving consecutive life sentences,

414
00:17:36,622 --> 00:17:38,691
but OK, see you.

415
00:17:39,425 --> 00:17:41,727
[Joel] Oh, it's been a good day.

416
00:17:44,830 --> 00:17:46,499
[Joel] You're a miracle worker, Wormy.

417
00:17:46,566 --> 00:17:49,468
-Feel better?
-That'll take a good night's sleep.

418
00:17:49,535 --> 00:17:51,003
Yeah.

419
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:52,872
They're gonna be sorry
for this, ain't they?

420
00:17:53,606 --> 00:17:55,808
Yes, little man, they'll be sorry.

421
00:17:55,875 --> 00:17:56,776
Want me to do it?

422
00:17:57,343 --> 00:17:58,411
Do what?

423
00:17:58,578 --> 00:17:59,545
Kill 'em.

424
00:18:00,146 --> 00:18:01,814
Not you, Jake. You're too stupid.

425
00:18:01,881 --> 00:18:02,815
[Crow] Well, I'm off the hook then.

426
00:18:02,882 --> 00:18:05,084
You'd be sure to get caught
and that would lead straight to me.

427
00:18:05,151 --> 00:18:07,086
Just as Nate Signo
was leading Scott Hood to me.

428
00:18:07,153 --> 00:18:08,220
No, no. I wouldn't get caught.

429
00:18:08,287 --> 00:18:09,722
I'm smarter than you think.
I'm real smart.

430
00:18:09,789 --> 00:18:11,324
Jake! You're hurting me.

431
00:18:11,390 --> 00:18:14,060
I didn't mean it, Erica.
I didn't mean it.

432
00:18:14,126 --> 00:18:15,895
All right, I forgive you.

433
00:18:15,962 --> 00:18:17,863
[Servo] So they really use their
Helen Gallagher catalog, huh?

434
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:18,931
I want you to do me a favor.

435
00:18:18,998 --> 00:18:20,499
Sure, what kind of favor?

436
00:18:20,566 --> 00:18:21,601
[Joel] Get a restraining order
on yourself.

437
00:18:21,667 --> 00:18:22,835
I want you to ride to Tombstone

438
00:18:22,902 --> 00:18:24,236
and pick me a new assistant.

439
00:18:24,303 --> 00:18:26,939
I'll pick you one. I'll pick the best.

440
00:18:27,239 --> 00:18:28,975
Maybe I can find Billy the Kid.

441
00:18:29,041 --> 00:18:30,710
I don't care who you get,

442
00:18:30,776 --> 00:18:32,678
just as long as he knows his business.

443
00:18:33,512 --> 00:18:35,147
I want him here within the week.

444
00:18:35,214 --> 00:18:37,083
[Crow] What kind of
salary are we offering?

445
00:18:37,149 --> 00:18:38,851
And benefits? Benefit--
I better write this down,

446
00:18:38,918 --> 00:18:40,720
that's going to be a lot of stuff.

447
00:18:41,787 --> 00:18:44,690
[Servo] ♪ It must be him
<i>It must be him ♪</i>

448
00:18:47,760 --> 00:18:49,328
[Joel as horse] Oh, no, not, Wormy.
Come on please.

449
00:18:49,395 --> 00:18:51,530
Don't get on me, Wormy, I can't...

450
00:18:51,597 --> 00:18:53,599
[Crow] The riveting
horse mounting scene.

451
00:18:55,101 --> 00:18:57,436
[Joel] Hey, nobody told me... Owie! Ow!

452
00:18:57,503 --> 00:18:59,238
[gunshots]

453
00:18:59,305 --> 00:19:00,172
[♪♪♪]

454
00:19:00,239 --> 00:19:02,875
[Servo]<i> ♪ Goldfinger ♪</i>

455
00:19:03,309 --> 00:19:05,578
<i>♪ Goldfinger ♪</i>

456
00:19:05,811 --> 00:19:08,214
<i>♪ Goldfinger ♪</i>

457
00:19:09,382 --> 00:19:11,150
[Joel] Tuesday, the rabbi got robbed.

458
00:19:12,752 --> 00:19:14,120
[gunshots]

459
00:19:14,186 --> 00:19:16,756
{\an8}[Crow] Well, I'm pretty sure
he was a bad guy, yeah.

460
00:19:17,890 --> 00:19:20,393
[Joel] He's a really fortunate lawman,

461
00:19:20,459 --> 00:19:22,561
he just walks right into crimes.

462
00:19:23,029 --> 00:19:24,830
[Servo] Yeah, I'll just take your lunch.

463
00:19:26,265 --> 00:19:28,167
[Crow] Boy, it's really blue out today.

464
00:19:30,136 --> 00:19:33,305
[Servo] ♪ Walk along the city streets
<i>We used to walk. ♪</i>

465
00:19:37,743 --> 00:19:40,413
[Crow] You know, shed a few pounds,
he's Mr. Drysdale.

466
00:19:42,048 --> 00:19:44,050
[Servo] Yeah, LaCroix please.

467
00:19:45,384 --> 00:19:47,787
Sorry, Mayor, it's after closing.

468
00:19:47,853 --> 00:19:49,088
I'm not here for a drink.

469
00:19:50,056 --> 00:19:51,257
What's the matter?

470
00:19:51,323 --> 00:19:52,658
Well, frankly, Erica, I'm worried.

471
00:19:52,725 --> 00:19:53,893
[Crow] Guess who wants
to be a rock star.

472
00:19:53,959 --> 00:19:55,461
Because I've been running around
with strange men?

473
00:19:55,528 --> 00:19:58,064
-Come on, now. I'm serious.
-[Joel] Where there's no one left alive.

474
00:19:58,130 --> 00:19:59,632
Do you realize how far
you've extended your nose

475
00:19:59,699 --> 00:20:00,866
in town property?

476
00:20:01,634 --> 00:20:03,602
I'm familiar with my business affairs.

477
00:20:04,103 --> 00:20:05,071
I've been down at the Land Office

478
00:20:05,137 --> 00:20:06,305
checking through the deed files.

479
00:20:06,372 --> 00:20:07,573
[Crow] I'm a research nut.

480
00:20:07,640 --> 00:20:10,076
Suddenly I notice the name
"Erica Page" everywhere.

481
00:20:10,509 --> 00:20:12,178
[Joel] Her face kind of
comes to a point.

482
00:20:12,244 --> 00:20:15,514
All right, Mayor,
I'll let you in on the big secret.

483
00:20:15,581 --> 00:20:17,083
[Servo] I'm Lonesome George Gobel...

484
00:20:17,149 --> 00:20:19,051
-[plate clatters; object thumps]
-[Servo] See?

485
00:20:19,118 --> 00:20:20,619
Let's have a drink.

486
00:20:20,686 --> 00:20:23,022
[Crow] All right,
DJ Swan Mellow Nights.

487
00:20:23,689 --> 00:20:26,792
[Servo] And that's when I became
known as Mr. Wiggly. You?

488
00:20:26,859 --> 00:20:28,160
Let me see if I got this straight.

489
00:20:28,227 --> 00:20:30,196
[Crow] You're a man playing
a woman playing a man.

490
00:20:30,262 --> 00:20:33,833
...out of business
and liquidate the inventory

491
00:20:33,899 --> 00:20:34,767
and the other assets

492
00:20:34,834 --> 00:20:37,002
and then use that money
to buy the next place.

493
00:20:37,503 --> 00:20:38,771
You're brilliant.

494
00:20:38,838 --> 00:20:40,639
Oh, it's just not possible.

495
00:20:40,706 --> 00:20:41,941
[Servo] Tell that to Dave Del Dotto.

496
00:20:42,041 --> 00:20:44,076
Have you noticed
how that line of property lies?

497
00:20:44,143 --> 00:20:45,344
[Joel] Don't you hate that?

498
00:20:45,411 --> 00:20:47,713
You said it looked
like a geometric pattern.

499
00:20:47,780 --> 00:20:49,915
Well, picture it in your mind's eye.

500
00:20:50,416 --> 00:20:52,852
[Crow] Oh, I get it, it's funny.

501
00:20:52,918 --> 00:20:54,186
Yeah. Oh, yeah. I see it now.

502
00:20:54,253 --> 00:20:55,554
[Servo] Yeah, baby, that's the way.

503
00:20:55,621 --> 00:20:57,556
It lies on the ground
that the Land Commission

504
00:20:57,623 --> 00:20:59,425
has picked out as a suggested right of way

505
00:20:59,492 --> 00:21:01,026
for the railroad and depot.

506
00:21:01,560 --> 00:21:02,695
[Erica] Exactly.

507
00:21:02,762 --> 00:21:03,696
[Joel] You mean, I am right?

508
00:21:03,763 --> 00:21:05,064
Oh, but Erica, this scheme of yours

509
00:21:05,131 --> 00:21:08,367
is the height of speculative gambling.

510
00:21:08,467 --> 00:21:10,603
The railroad decides
not to build through Oracle,

511
00:21:10,669 --> 00:21:11,670
you'll be wiped out.

512
00:21:11,737 --> 00:21:14,173
-[Servo] Phooey on youey. [spits]
-It's a chance.

513
00:21:14,240 --> 00:21:15,841
An extremely long one.

514
00:21:16,442 --> 00:21:19,211
[Crow] Well, I got to hit my shift
at the Roy Rogers.

515
00:21:19,278 --> 00:21:21,781
Well, I want those trains
to come through, too,

516
00:21:22,047 --> 00:21:25,584
and I guess we'll get the decision
in Saturday's postal express.

517
00:21:27,286 --> 00:21:29,722
'Course you realize
how the town'll feel if...

518
00:21:29,822 --> 00:21:32,324
Some nights I lie awake
two or three seconds

519
00:21:32,391 --> 00:21:34,360
-worrying about it.
-[Servo] Oops, sorry.

520
00:21:34,426 --> 00:21:35,661
Goodnight, Mayor.

521
00:21:36,662 --> 00:21:40,966
Goodnight, Erica, and, uh, good luck.

522
00:21:41,033 --> 00:21:42,501
[Crow] Thanks for the drinks and stuff.

523
00:21:42,568 --> 00:21:44,837
Sorry, I was such the pig with a Chex Mix.

524
00:21:46,338 --> 00:21:48,974
[Joel] Looks like he's been
in the little man's room there.

525
00:21:49,041 --> 00:21:51,744
...Tombstone. Got the man you wanted.

526
00:21:52,945 --> 00:21:54,713
<i>I got the best.</i>

527
00:21:54,780 --> 00:21:56,816
-What's his name?
-Cane Miro.

528
00:22:05,591 --> 00:22:07,827
♪<i> Rum, dum, da-dum </i>♪

529
00:22:07,893 --> 00:22:10,095
♪<i> Dum, dum, dum, dum... </i>♪

530
00:22:10,162 --> 00:22:12,164
So, this is what it's like to be dead.

531
00:22:12,231 --> 00:22:15,201
Well, roughly this is what
it's like to be in a casket.

532
00:22:15,267 --> 00:22:17,236
So, why are we doing this?

533
00:22:17,303 --> 00:22:18,470
Aren't you curious?

534
00:22:18,537 --> 00:22:19,772
About being dead?

535
00:22:19,839 --> 00:22:21,006
We're robots, Joel.

536
00:22:21,073 --> 00:22:22,508
We're not the ones
who have to worry about it.

537
00:22:22,575 --> 00:22:23,976
Uh, you understand my point?

538
00:22:24,043 --> 00:22:25,744
Oh, yeah, well, at least
I have a soul, OK.

539
00:22:25,811 --> 00:22:26,879
Yeah, sure you do.

540
00:22:26,946 --> 00:22:30,783
Anyway, even though I'm not going to die,
I sure could see having a snappy funeral.

541
00:22:30,850 --> 00:22:32,451
Not like the one in the movie though.

542
00:22:32,518 --> 00:22:33,552
What a drag!

543
00:22:33,619 --> 00:22:34,620
Oh, at my funeral,

544
00:22:34,687 --> 00:22:36,255
I'd hope my friends
would toss me up and down

545
00:22:36,322 --> 00:22:38,324
in a blanket like the Eskimos do,
you know?

546
00:22:38,390 --> 00:22:39,391
Really go for some height.

547
00:22:39,458 --> 00:22:40,659
Ooh. Well, how about a beach funeral?

548
00:22:40,726 --> 00:22:42,494
You know, pony keg, bonfire,

549
00:22:42,561 --> 00:22:45,164
couple slipping off
into the woods to neck.

550
00:22:45,231 --> 00:22:46,866
Prop me up so I can surf.

551
00:22:46,932 --> 00:22:48,868
Hey, I'd go the dignity route.

552
00:22:48,934 --> 00:22:50,603
You know, variety of ethnic foods

553
00:22:50,669 --> 00:22:52,872
or maybe a saxophone quartet.

554
00:22:52,938 --> 00:22:54,206
Dignity, smignity, Joel.

555
00:22:54,273 --> 00:22:55,641
I want elephants, lots of them,

556
00:22:55,708 --> 00:22:57,943
and circus ladies as my pallbearers.

557
00:22:58,010 --> 00:22:59,211
I want them enthusiastic

558
00:22:59,278 --> 00:23:02,181
and wearing those little frilly skirts
as little tutus.

559
00:23:02,248 --> 00:23:04,850
You know, Tom,
cost could be a consideration.

560
00:23:04,917 --> 00:23:06,485
Oh, nonsense, Joel.

561
00:23:06,552 --> 00:23:07,853
I'll lie in state for several days

562
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:09,822
at the Corn Palace
while "Hooked On a Feeling"

563
00:23:09,889 --> 00:23:11,824
is sung by a choir of castrati.

564
00:23:11,891 --> 00:23:13,959
You know, there's always
the educational route,

565
00:23:14,026 --> 00:23:15,694
so a real hands-on kind of funeral,

566
00:23:15,761 --> 00:23:18,797
details of my embalming
written up and distributed.

567
00:23:18,864 --> 00:23:22,401
-It is fun to think about it.
-It sure is.

568
00:23:22,935 --> 00:23:26,505
So, uh, when you humans die,
that's it, right, uh...

569
00:23:26,572 --> 00:23:27,640
you're dead forever?

570
00:23:27,706 --> 00:23:28,574
Yeah.

571
00:23:28,641 --> 00:23:29,909
Well, isn't that like
throwing the baby out

572
00:23:29,975 --> 00:23:31,243
with the bath water, Joel?

573
00:23:31,310 --> 00:23:33,612
Why don't you just not die, Joel?

574
00:23:33,679 --> 00:23:34,847
Well, everybody dies.

575
00:23:34,914 --> 00:23:37,917
Oh, and if everybody ran
off a cliff, you'd do that too?

576
00:23:37,983 --> 00:23:39,685
Well, that's not the way it works,

577
00:23:39,752 --> 00:23:41,520
besides we got commercials sign.

578
00:23:41,587 --> 00:23:43,222
Well, it's just weird, that's all.

579
00:23:43,289 --> 00:23:44,590
Maybe it's us.

580
00:23:44,657 --> 00:23:46,358
Joel, is there any way
I could be mummified

581
00:23:46,425 --> 00:23:48,027
and placed next to Stalin?

582
00:23:48,093 --> 00:23:49,194
Sure, honey.

583
00:23:49,261 --> 00:23:50,429
Well, that's what I want,

584
00:23:50,496 --> 00:23:52,531
mummified and placed next to Stalin.

585
00:23:53,565 --> 00:23:55,367
<i>[humming] ♪ Dum dum ba dum ♪</i>

586
00:23:55,434 --> 00:23:57,303
<i>♪ Bum ba dum dum dum dum ♪</i>

587
00:23:57,369 --> 00:23:59,071
<i>♪ Da da da</i>
<i>Dum da dum da dum ♪</i>

588
00:23:59,138 --> 00:24:00,172
<i>♪ Dum da da ♪</i>

589
00:24:03,008 --> 00:24:04,843
[Joel] Yeah, death sucks.

590
00:24:06,545 --> 00:24:08,180
[Crow] Yeah, I don't even want
to know what I stepped in.

591
00:24:08,247 --> 00:24:09,682
[gunshots]

592
00:24:11,250 --> 00:24:13,352
[Joel] Jeepers, it's hard
to get into this town.

593
00:24:13,419 --> 00:24:15,120
[Rose] Stop it, mister.
I've got you cold.

594
00:24:15,187 --> 00:24:16,689
[Crow] Yep, she does.

595
00:24:21,927 --> 00:24:22,895
[Servo] Say...

596
00:24:22,962 --> 00:24:23,896
Whaddya know?

597
00:24:24,930 --> 00:24:26,131
A lady with a star.

598
00:24:26,198 --> 00:24:28,734
[Servo] ♪ You can dust your car
<i>To the lady with the star ♪</i>

599
00:24:28,801 --> 00:24:30,669
You're not the man I'm after.

600
00:24:30,736 --> 00:24:32,504
-I'm sorry.
-[Joel] I'm really sorry.

601
00:24:32,571 --> 00:24:34,173
I'm sorry I took a shot at you.

602
00:24:34,239 --> 00:24:36,275
-[Crow] That's one on me.
-My name's Rose Hood.

603
00:24:36,342 --> 00:24:37,309
Cane Miro.

604
00:24:37,376 --> 00:24:39,979
-Any relation to John Miro?
-Cane Miro?

605
00:24:40,045 --> 00:24:41,280
Well, that sounds familiar.

606
00:24:41,780 --> 00:24:43,549
I don't think we've met.

607
00:24:43,615 --> 00:24:45,884
If we had, I'd have remembered.

608
00:24:45,951 --> 00:24:47,853
I'm the marshal here.
I'm glad I missed you.

609
00:24:47,920 --> 00:24:50,022
I was aiming at a killer
I meaned to catch.

610
00:24:50,089 --> 00:24:51,090
[Joel] There he goes now.

611
00:24:51,156 --> 00:24:52,624
I'd like to help you, ma'am.

612
00:24:52,691 --> 00:24:54,560
Well, he's supposed to be
hiding out in Nine Mile Canyon.

613
00:24:54,626 --> 00:24:56,328
[Crow] How long is that canyon?

614
00:24:56,395 --> 00:24:57,796
As a matter of fact, I did see some smoke

615
00:24:57,863 --> 00:25:00,399
coming up from the deep canyon brush.

616
00:25:00,466 --> 00:25:03,035
Can't imagine
an honest man living down there.

617
00:25:03,102 --> 00:25:04,236
No, neither can I.

618
00:25:04,803 --> 00:25:05,838
-Let's go.
-Go?

619
00:25:05,904 --> 00:25:07,206
[Joel] Yeah, go.

620
00:25:07,272 --> 00:25:08,741
We have to get him, don't we?

621
00:25:08,807 --> 00:25:10,175
[Servo] Oh, oh. "Go."

622
00:25:10,909 --> 00:25:13,445
I guess we do. I'll just get my horse.

623
00:25:13,512 --> 00:25:15,047
[Servo] Well, since we're going...

624
00:25:17,149 --> 00:25:19,385
[Crow] Hey, Cane, who is the girl?

625
00:25:22,154 --> 00:25:24,556
[Joel as horse] Hey, watch it,
your hands are cold.

626
00:25:24,623 --> 00:25:25,891
[horse snorts]

627
00:25:28,260 --> 00:25:30,863
[Servo] Hey, I love what
you're driving. A Pinto, right?

628
00:25:33,499 --> 00:25:35,868
[Crow] Let's ride separately,
I just feel more comfortable

629
00:25:35,934 --> 00:25:37,770
if we rode separately.

630
00:25:37,836 --> 00:25:39,004
I'm winning.

631
00:25:40,639 --> 00:25:42,574
[Servo] No, no, I'm winning.

632
00:25:42,641 --> 00:25:43,876
[Joel] Yeah, I let you though.

633
00:25:48,447 --> 00:25:50,616
[Cane] You wait here.
I'll look around.

634
00:25:53,452 --> 00:25:54,686
[Crow] Now, where's he going?

635
00:25:54,753 --> 00:25:56,155
I'm as nervous as a long tail cat

636
00:25:56,221 --> 00:25:57,956
in a room full of rocking chairs.

637
00:25:59,124 --> 00:26:01,060
[Servo] Sir, you got a permit?

638
00:26:01,126 --> 00:26:03,128
I notice you don't have
a ticket on your post.

639
00:26:03,195 --> 00:26:05,631
Hello? sir?

640
00:26:07,733 --> 00:26:11,003
[Joel] Oh, come on, everyone knows
that there are no hot plates

641
00:26:11,070 --> 00:26:13,539
allowed in Nine Mile Canyon.

642
00:26:16,175 --> 00:26:17,776
[Crow] Now, where are you going?

643
00:26:17,843 --> 00:26:19,344
[Crow crying]

644
00:26:19,411 --> 00:26:20,813
Stay with me.

645
00:26:20,879 --> 00:26:22,247
[Servo] Well, there's three bowls
of porridge here,

646
00:26:22,314 --> 00:26:23,782
don't quite know what that means.

647
00:26:25,717 --> 00:26:29,154
[Joel] You know, I like it, honey,
I think we should make an offer.

648
00:26:29,221 --> 00:26:30,089
He's around.

649
00:26:31,023 --> 00:26:31,957
Where?

650
00:26:32,024 --> 00:26:33,859
[Servo] I'm in the outhouse,
I'll be right back out.

651
00:26:33,926 --> 00:26:36,195
...getting more water for these potatoes.

652
00:26:36,261 --> 00:26:39,331
-[Crow] So, he's Irish, huh?
-Uh-huh. So what do we do?

653
00:26:39,398 --> 00:26:40,933
[Joel] We could start the salad.

654
00:26:40,999 --> 00:26:42,101
Wait in there.

655
00:26:42,167 --> 00:26:43,735
[Joel] Cover me, I'll set the table.

656
00:26:46,405 --> 00:26:49,475
[Servo] We'll hide behind this tree.
Are you sure you're the best?

657
00:26:51,009 --> 00:26:52,311
Alright now, how do you want him?

658
00:26:52,377 --> 00:26:53,579
[Joel] Lady's choice.

659
00:26:53,645 --> 00:26:56,448
-Alive.
-[Crow] Why? How do you want him?

660
00:26:56,515 --> 00:26:58,417
Where do you come from, Mr. Miro?

661
00:26:58,917 --> 00:27:00,819
Lately, mostly from around Tombstone.

662
00:27:00,886 --> 00:27:02,354
[Servo] Before that,
Medford, Wisconsin.

663
00:27:02,421 --> 00:27:03,455
[Rose] Pretty rough place.

664
00:27:04,223 --> 00:27:05,791
That's what they tell me.

665
00:27:06,525 --> 00:27:08,894
Still trying to figure out
where I've heard of you.

666
00:27:09,194 --> 00:27:10,629
It'll come.

667
00:27:10,696 --> 00:27:11,697
Were you in the war?

668
00:27:12,865 --> 00:27:14,266
-Bragg's Army.
-[Crow] Pastry chef.

669
00:27:14,333 --> 00:27:15,534
That was a long time ago.

670
00:27:16,068 --> 00:27:17,436
Not according to our good mayor.

671
00:27:17,503 --> 00:27:19,438
For him, the South is still winning.

672
00:27:19,505 --> 00:27:21,306
Gideon Polk?

673
00:27:21,373 --> 00:27:22,407
You know him?

674
00:27:23,175 --> 00:27:25,310
Captain Polk and I are old Army friends.

675
00:27:25,377 --> 00:27:27,112
[Servo] Look, let's just focus on
our stakeout right now.

676
00:27:27,179 --> 00:27:29,148
He's my main reason for coming to Oracle.

677
00:27:30,048 --> 00:27:31,750
Except maybe now,
I've found a better one.

678
00:27:31,817 --> 00:27:34,386
-[horse whinnies]
-[Joel] Hey, it's Bigfoot with a bucket.

679
00:27:36,121 --> 00:27:38,257
[Servo] Hi, folks, welcome
to my lien too. [spits]

680
00:27:39,758 --> 00:27:41,527
-Nice day.
-[Crow] Nice day.

681
00:27:41,593 --> 00:27:43,962
I'm arresting you
for the murder of Uriah Baker.

682
00:27:44,029 --> 00:27:45,130
Drop your gun belt.

683
00:27:46,198 --> 00:27:47,399
[Joel] I said your gun belt.

684
00:27:47,466 --> 00:27:48,700
I'd also like to have
a little talk with you

685
00:27:48,767 --> 00:27:50,669
about your connection with Erica Page.

686
00:27:52,004 --> 00:27:53,572
I'm gonna talk, I'm gonna ride.

687
00:27:53,639 --> 00:27:54,840
Keep your mouth shut.

688
00:27:55,774 --> 00:27:57,042
I'll keep him covered, Marshal.

689
00:27:57,109 --> 00:27:58,911
How 'bout you dousing the fire.

690
00:27:58,977 --> 00:28:01,680
[Servo] You know, the way you do?
I'd like that.

691
00:28:05,684 --> 00:28:07,853
[Crow] I was just going
to get your potato.

692
00:28:07,920 --> 00:28:09,254
That happened faster than it could have.

693
00:28:09,321 --> 00:28:10,722
[Joel] Over the speed of light.

694
00:28:10,789 --> 00:28:11,757
Yes, ma'am.

695
00:28:13,192 --> 00:28:14,626
Come on.

696
00:28:14,693 --> 00:28:17,129
I'll help you get your worm bait
back to beyond.

697
00:28:17,196 --> 00:28:18,197
[piano music playing]

698
00:28:18,263 --> 00:28:21,233
[Servo] Oh, stop.
Quick, charley horse! Oh, ow...

699
00:28:23,135 --> 00:28:25,871
[Crow] Yes,
<i>Buns of Steel of the Old West.</i>

700
00:28:25,938 --> 00:28:28,373
[Servo] And naughty spank
and naughty spink,

701
00:28:28,440 --> 00:28:30,442
and you've been bad in the tushie.

702
00:28:30,509 --> 00:28:32,578
Now, naughty, naughty, naughty

703
00:28:32,644 --> 00:28:35,414
and naughty, naughty, naughty this way,

704
00:28:35,480 --> 00:28:37,182
naughty, naughty, naughty,

705
00:28:37,249 --> 00:28:39,885
and naughty, naughty, naughty, that way.

706
00:28:39,952 --> 00:28:41,286
Higher, girls.

707
00:28:42,087 --> 00:28:44,556
[Crow] Say what you want, Reverend,
this brings in the parishioners.

708
00:28:46,158 --> 00:28:47,392
[Servo] Whee...

709
00:28:47,459 --> 00:28:49,828
Oh, look at them poor girls there.

710
00:28:50,095 --> 00:28:53,332
Do you know that Mrs. Marshal Hood's
ordered them out of town?

711
00:28:53,398 --> 00:28:55,467
She says they constitute
an "immoral influence"

712
00:28:55,534 --> 00:28:57,069
-on our young men.
-[laughing]

713
00:28:57,169 --> 00:28:58,804
[Servo] That's pretty much
the idea, isn't it?

714
00:28:59,338 --> 00:29:01,673
[♪♪♪]

715
00:29:01,740 --> 00:29:04,977
[Crow] Joel, you know, it's so good
you almost forget it's erotic.

716
00:29:05,043 --> 00:29:07,212
[Joel] ♪ Shuffle Off the Buffalo
<i>Shuffle Off the Buffalo ♪</i>

717
00:29:07,279 --> 00:29:08,380
<i>♪ And stick the butt up... ♪</i>

718
00:29:08,447 --> 00:29:10,415
[Joel] Yeah, remember,
when we were part of the act, Jed?

719
00:29:10,482 --> 00:29:12,985
They said I didn't glide quite right.

720
00:29:14,253 --> 00:29:15,187
[applause]

721
00:29:15,254 --> 00:29:17,122
Hear they gotta be out by Friday.

722
00:29:17,189 --> 00:29:19,191
-Friday noon.
-[Servo] Whatever.

723
00:29:19,992 --> 00:29:22,828
Somebody's always tryin'
to push somebody else out.

724
00:29:22,894 --> 00:29:24,696
Like the Yankees trying
to push us out of Georgia.

725
00:29:24,763 --> 00:29:25,831
[all three] Shut up.

726
00:29:25,897 --> 00:29:27,432
Looks to me they accomplished that.

727
00:29:27,499 --> 00:29:29,101
Not at first, they didn't.

728
00:29:29,835 --> 00:29:30,769
You should've been with me at...

729
00:29:30,836 --> 00:29:32,170
[Crow] Excuse me, who is talking?

730
00:29:32,237 --> 00:29:35,040
...smash Grant and Rose
plans at the Googleberg.

731
00:29:35,107 --> 00:29:36,041
[Joel] Googleberg?

732
00:29:36,108 --> 00:29:37,976
Let's see, uh, you were in the artillery

733
00:29:38,043 --> 00:29:39,144
by then, weren't you?

734
00:29:39,211 --> 00:29:40,646
Yes, sir.

735
00:29:40,712 --> 00:29:41,847
[Servo] You were a bootblack.

736
00:29:41,913 --> 00:29:44,683
...shot rounds and canisters
as fast as we could load.

737
00:29:44,750 --> 00:29:47,853
Why, he handled them guns
like they was red-hot stovepipes.

738
00:29:47,919 --> 00:29:50,656
How well did you handle them
at Lookout Mountain, Captain Polk?

739
00:29:50,722 --> 00:29:52,791
[Servo imitating Ronald Reagan]
Hell, I don't recall,

740
00:29:52,858 --> 00:29:54,259
I don't recall.

741
00:29:54,326 --> 00:29:56,695
[Joel] Mr. Mooneys
of the Old West.

742
00:29:56,762 --> 00:29:57,996
Private Cane Miro.

743
00:29:59,197 --> 00:30:00,465
It is you.

744
00:30:01,633 --> 00:30:03,468
You've got a good memory.

745
00:30:03,535 --> 00:30:05,304
But then, that was something
no one could forget,

746
00:30:05,370 --> 00:30:06,405
wasn't it, Captain?

747
00:30:06,471 --> 00:30:07,639
[Crow] That he's got a good memory?

748
00:30:07,706 --> 00:30:08,840
I thought you were dead.

749
00:30:09,274 --> 00:30:10,609
The good die first.

750
00:30:10,676 --> 00:30:12,311
[Servo] Most people
are morally ambiguous,

751
00:30:12,377 --> 00:30:14,546
which explains our random dying patterns.

752
00:30:14,613 --> 00:30:17,049
I understand you're a good citizen.

753
00:30:17,115 --> 00:30:18,483
[Joel] Now that's
a complex death threat.

754
00:30:18,550 --> 00:30:19,851
Why'd you come here?

755
00:30:19,918 --> 00:30:21,386
Well, goodnight, Mayor.

756
00:30:21,453 --> 00:30:22,387
Goodnight, Erica.

757
00:30:22,454 --> 00:30:23,488
We'll wind up our business tomorrow.

758
00:30:23,588 --> 00:30:25,991
-[Crow] Let me call you a cab.
-Don't leave.

759
00:30:26,058 --> 00:30:27,259
Are you afraid, Captain?

760
00:30:28,427 --> 00:30:31,096
How can one man help you
when 30,000 couldn't?

761
00:30:31,163 --> 00:30:32,331
[Servo] He makes a good point.

762
00:30:32,397 --> 00:30:33,365
Hello, Cane.

763
00:30:34,232 --> 00:30:35,434
Hello, Erica.

764
00:30:36,668 --> 00:30:37,736
It's been a long time.

765
00:30:37,803 --> 00:30:39,738
[Servo] It's been a long, long,
long, long lonely time.

766
00:30:39,805 --> 00:30:40,906
I wouldn't touch 'em.

767
00:30:40,972 --> 00:30:42,974
-[Crow] With all that makeup.
-Come on with me, Gideon.

768
00:30:44,009 --> 00:30:45,544
You better retreat, Mayor.

769
00:30:46,411 --> 00:30:48,013
I'll see you another day.

770
00:30:48,980 --> 00:30:50,382
Goodnight, Cane.

771
00:30:50,449 --> 00:30:52,384
-Goodnight, Erica.
-[Joel] Boy, the Mayor's approval rating

772
00:30:52,451 --> 00:30:54,119
just plunged like 20 points.

773
00:30:54,186 --> 00:30:55,320
-[Servo] Yeah.
-[Crow] Whoa.

774
00:30:55,387 --> 00:30:56,455
What was that all about?

775
00:30:56,521 --> 00:30:58,090
[Servo] You know, it's tough,
we used to be roommates.

776
00:30:58,156 --> 00:30:59,157
It's a long story.

777
00:30:59,257 --> 00:31:01,793
Well, leave him alone. I need him.

778
00:31:01,860 --> 00:31:03,028
So do I.

779
00:31:03,729 --> 00:31:05,564
Now tell me why you sent for me.

780
00:31:05,897 --> 00:31:08,266
Your friend here said something
about a killing.

781
00:31:08,333 --> 00:31:09,401
[Crow] Who needs me?

782
00:31:09,468 --> 00:31:10,535
Who needs Wormy?

783
00:31:11,269 --> 00:31:12,337
We have to talk shop here?

784
00:31:12,404 --> 00:31:14,606
[Joel] Old Western art of the Old West.

785
00:31:14,673 --> 00:31:16,141
Come on into my dressing room.

786
00:31:19,311 --> 00:31:21,947
[Joel] And I don't like him.

787
00:31:25,150 --> 00:31:28,019
[Crow] That's a line that Miss Kitty
and Matthew never crossed.

788
00:31:28,086 --> 00:31:29,054
Jake was right.

789
00:31:29,721 --> 00:31:30,789
A killing.

790
00:31:32,858 --> 00:31:33,792
Now, kiss me, Cane.

791
00:31:33,859 --> 00:31:34,926
[Servo] By Cole Porter.

792
00:31:34,993 --> 00:31:36,194
Make it like old times.

793
00:31:36,261 --> 00:31:37,629
[Servo] Well, you mean,
like after the football game

794
00:31:37,696 --> 00:31:38,897
out by the dumpster...?

795
00:31:38,964 --> 00:31:39,965
[Servo muffled speech]

796
00:31:40,599 --> 00:31:42,134
[Crow] You got a wood tick there,
let me get a match.

797
00:31:42,200 --> 00:31:44,269
Who do I kill? The brave captain?

798
00:31:44,336 --> 00:31:45,337
[Servo] Is he getting shorter?

799
00:31:45,404 --> 00:31:47,739
Jake, this man has
no romance in his soul.

800
00:31:48,807 --> 00:31:50,342
Maybe you kill nobody.

801
00:31:50,409 --> 00:31:52,377
I didn't come up here
just to make it like old times.

802
00:31:52,444 --> 00:31:54,880
-[Joel] Whoa.
-And I get paid in advance.

803
00:31:56,248 --> 00:31:58,650
Jake, get 3,000 out of the office safe.

804
00:31:58,717 --> 00:31:59,951
Take your time doing that.

805
00:32:00,018 --> 00:32:02,487
[Crow] If looks could kill you,
you'd be so almost dead.

806
00:32:03,021 --> 00:32:04,189
[door slams]

807
00:32:04,256 --> 00:32:05,123
That's better.

808
00:32:05,590 --> 00:32:06,892
No point in my having to trust you

809
00:32:06,958 --> 00:32:09,027
when I can worry about nicer things.

810
00:32:09,694 --> 00:32:10,796
What things, Cane?

811
00:32:10,862 --> 00:32:13,598
[Servo] Raindrops on roses,
whiskers on kittens.

812
00:32:13,965 --> 00:32:15,967
...who do I kill and when?

813
00:32:17,335 --> 00:32:18,503
The local law.

814
00:32:18,570 --> 00:32:20,672
[Joel] Oh, get a room... Oh, they did.

815
00:32:20,739 --> 00:32:22,541
[Crow] Hmm, chocolaty.

816
00:32:24,976 --> 00:32:26,511
Why wait 'til Saturday?

817
00:32:28,046 --> 00:32:31,683
On Saturday, the mayor gets a letter
from the railroad board of directors,

818
00:32:31,750 --> 00:32:34,152
letting the town know
if the new tracks come through here.

819
00:32:34,219 --> 00:32:35,287
[Servo] Is that a euphemism?

820
00:32:35,353 --> 00:32:36,321
If they do, I clean up.

821
00:32:36,388 --> 00:32:39,224
-[Servo] I think that's a euphemism.
-Maybe you won't have to kill Mrs. Hood.

822
00:32:40,158 --> 00:32:43,328
If they don't, I'll have to grab
all the money I can and clear out fast.

823
00:32:43,728 --> 00:32:44,763
There'll be killings.

824
00:32:44,830 --> 00:32:46,331
[Crow] This is more
than I want to know.

825
00:32:46,398 --> 00:32:48,467
I want the marshal
to be the first to die.

826
00:32:48,533 --> 00:32:50,936
[Joel] Oh, yeah, give me
more exposition.

827
00:32:51,002 --> 00:32:51,937
...if you like.

828
00:32:52,571 --> 00:32:53,705
Thanks for the bonus.

829
00:32:54,673 --> 00:32:56,241
So much for business.

830
00:32:56,308 --> 00:32:57,609
Let's get down to pleasure.

831
00:32:57,676 --> 00:32:59,077
[Crow] Some bonus.

832
00:33:01,379 --> 00:33:04,115
[Servo] Well, got down to pleasure.
Quite pleasurable.

833
00:33:04,182 --> 00:33:05,116
Remember me?

834
00:33:05,183 --> 00:33:08,186
[Joel] You were
on<i> Carter Country </i>, weren't you?

835
00:33:09,521 --> 00:33:10,622
Cane Miro.

836
00:33:10,689 --> 00:33:12,724
Wanted in three states
and five territories

837
00:33:12,791 --> 00:33:14,526
for murder, bank robbery, stage robbery,

838
00:33:14,593 --> 00:33:16,661
train robbery and sundry assault.

839
00:33:16,728 --> 00:33:17,662
[Servo] Neat.

840
00:33:17,729 --> 00:33:19,865
Take a look at your ledger.
See if I'm wanted in this state.

841
00:33:19,931 --> 00:33:21,032
I haven't checked lately.

842
00:33:21,099 --> 00:33:22,200
[Crow] My computer is down.

843
00:33:22,267 --> 00:33:23,134
[clacking]

844
00:33:23,201 --> 00:33:24,503
You ought to keep these clean.

845
00:33:26,238 --> 00:33:27,606
No, you're not wanted here.

846
00:33:28,340 --> 00:33:29,641
If you were, I'd find a place for you

847
00:33:29,708 --> 00:33:31,042
with the other characters I met this week.

848
00:33:31,109 --> 00:33:33,245
-[Joel] Here, wipe your nose.
-...my husband on Boot Hill.

849
00:33:33,311 --> 00:33:34,746
-Boot Hill?
-[Crow] So, you're single?

850
00:33:34,813 --> 00:33:36,615
Where everyone
sleeps together like kinfolk.

851
00:33:36,681 --> 00:33:37,983
[Joel] Not my kinfolk.

852
00:33:38,049 --> 00:33:39,150
...difference between 'em.

853
00:33:39,784 --> 00:33:42,120
Well, the bandits
usually get there first.

854
00:33:42,187 --> 00:33:44,155
Everyone gets there sooner or later.

855
00:33:44,222 --> 00:33:45,323
I'm not worried.

856
00:33:45,423 --> 00:33:46,958
[Servo] Anyway, the good
die first, you know.

857
00:33:47,025 --> 00:33:48,426
I'm going to get there
in the next five minutes.

858
00:33:50,161 --> 00:33:51,696
What's your business in Oracle?

859
00:33:51,796 --> 00:33:52,664
[Joel] Herbal Life.

860
00:33:52,731 --> 00:33:54,833
It's honest. It's also private.

861
00:33:54,900 --> 00:33:57,135
Heh. Well, that's no answer.

862
00:33:57,669 --> 00:33:59,137
I intend to keep it that way.

863
00:33:59,237 --> 00:34:00,839
[Crow] Not exactly
a Howard Hawks film, is it?

864
00:34:00,906 --> 00:34:02,307
How long's it going to
take you to finish it up?

865
00:34:02,908 --> 00:34:04,609
Oh, about five weeks.

866
00:34:05,810 --> 00:34:06,711
Make it five days?

867
00:34:06,778 --> 00:34:09,147
[Joel] What are they negotiating,
when he's going to kill her?

868
00:34:09,915 --> 00:34:12,183
I might be able to finish in five days,

869
00:34:12,250 --> 00:34:14,419
but that also gives me five nights.

870
00:34:14,486 --> 00:34:16,087
What do you do nights, Miss Marshal?

871
00:34:16,154 --> 00:34:17,889
[Crow] Oh, I run
like a crazed weasel. You?

872
00:34:17,956 --> 00:34:21,026
Oh, I keep an eye
on suspicious characters.

873
00:34:21,793 --> 00:34:24,095
-I'm a suspicious character.
-[Joel mockingly laughs]

874
00:34:24,162 --> 00:34:26,831
I think I'll assign Joshua to you.
He takes care of drunks,

875
00:34:26,898 --> 00:34:28,600
mad dogs, and smart saddle tramps.

876
00:34:28,667 --> 00:34:30,568
-[Crow] And Englishmen.
-[But] I'm a celebrity.

877
00:34:31,236 --> 00:34:33,038
You ought to give me
your personal attention.

878
00:34:33,138 --> 00:34:34,806
[Servo] I was up
for a CableACE Award.

879
00:34:35,407 --> 00:34:37,342
I just hope I don't have to, Mr. Miro.

880
00:34:37,876 --> 00:34:39,945
[Joel] Well, I'm going to shut down
the sexual bantering

881
00:34:40,011 --> 00:34:40,946
for the night.

882
00:34:42,914 --> 00:34:43,848
[Servo] Oh, boy!

883
00:34:44,616 --> 00:34:45,951
[Joel] Oh, Beverly!

884
00:34:49,321 --> 00:34:50,689
[Crow] Is this is a video diary?

885
00:34:50,755 --> 00:34:51,823
[Servo] Looks like a Kubrick film.

886
00:34:51,890 --> 00:34:54,826
{\an8}[Joel] I don't know, it doesn't
seem like a Tuesday.

887
00:34:56,828 --> 00:34:58,930
[Servo] Oh, back to Monday, May 31st.

888
00:34:58,997 --> 00:35:03,034
...ninety, ninety-five, fifteen thousand.

889
00:35:03,535 --> 00:35:06,271
Well, it's all there.

890
00:35:06,338 --> 00:35:07,339
[Crow] Enjoy your timeshare.

891
00:35:07,405 --> 00:35:08,640
I'll mail you your first monthly payment

892
00:35:08,707 --> 00:35:10,075
after you get to Santa Fe.

893
00:35:10,141 --> 00:35:11,509
[Joel] You know, back then,
money was a lot of money.

894
00:35:11,576 --> 00:35:13,511
Huh, now that the deal is closed,

895
00:35:13,578 --> 00:35:16,281
I don't mind telling you
that I got the best of the bargain.

896
00:35:16,881 --> 00:35:18,583
A widened freight line
won't do you much good

897
00:35:18,650 --> 00:35:21,519
when the railroad comes,
and if it doesn't,

898
00:35:21,586 --> 00:35:25,323
this town will have the business
of a steamboat in Death Valley.

899
00:35:25,390 --> 00:35:26,391
[Joel] Ha, I'm funny.

900
00:35:26,458 --> 00:35:28,126
Have you ever met a woman
with a head for business?

901
00:35:28,193 --> 00:35:29,527
[chuckling] Afraid not.

902
00:35:29,594 --> 00:35:31,029
Well, neither have I, Mister Taft.

903
00:35:31,963 --> 00:35:32,998
Have a nice trip.

904
00:35:33,064 --> 00:35:34,833
I'll be riding the high road.

905
00:35:34,899 --> 00:35:36,301
[Servo] William Howard Taft,
ladies and gentlemen.

906
00:35:36,368 --> 00:35:37,636
[Crow whistles]

907
00:35:38,637 --> 00:35:40,572
Nice of him to tell us
he's takin' the high road, huh?

908
00:35:40,639 --> 00:35:42,507
[Servo with feminine voice]
It's a figure of speech, Wormy.

909
00:35:42,574 --> 00:35:44,309
I wish I could send Cane on this.

910
00:35:44,376 --> 00:35:46,177
He won't take any of these puny jobs.

911
00:35:46,778 --> 00:35:49,681
Besides, why pay for something
I'll do for free?

912
00:35:49,748 --> 00:35:50,815
[Crow] Wormy, that's an old cedar.

913
00:35:50,882 --> 00:35:52,283
If you ever get caught,
they'll come after me.

914
00:35:52,917 --> 00:35:54,653
That's why I try to keep you
from sin, little man.

915
00:35:54,719 --> 00:35:56,721
-Did you marry the ketchup bottles?
-[slams wooden post]

916
00:35:57,455 --> 00:36:00,191
Cane Miro's mighty handy
with the women, isn't he?

917
00:36:00,258 --> 00:36:01,760
[Servo in feminine voice] Mighty.

918
00:36:01,826 --> 00:36:04,095
You don't love him.
You still love me, don't you, Erica?

919
00:36:04,696 --> 00:36:06,297
I still love you, Jake.

920
00:36:06,364 --> 00:36:07,766
Now you'd better hurry
if you want to catch Tab

921
00:36:07,832 --> 00:36:08,900
on the high road.

922
00:36:09,467 --> 00:36:12,570
I need that 15,000
to buy the Canby Judd place.

923
00:36:12,637 --> 00:36:14,239
I'll hurry. I'll fly!

924
00:36:14,305 --> 00:36:15,974
[Servo with nasally voice]
She thinks I'm cute!

925
00:36:18,043 --> 00:36:20,145
[Joel] Oh, man,
that American hotel

926
00:36:20,211 --> 00:36:22,347
puts on a great buffet on roadies.

927
00:36:23,048 --> 00:36:25,750
Back in, Herman.
You're becoming a real habit.

928
00:36:25,817 --> 00:36:27,585
[Crow with old man voice]
Yeah, don't fool with me, I'm a wizard.

929
00:36:27,652 --> 00:36:29,587
There goes that outlander, Cane Miro.

930
00:36:29,654 --> 00:36:31,556
I don't like him.
He's bound to be trouble.

931
00:36:31,623 --> 00:36:32,857
[Servo] He pushed me down.

932
00:36:34,759 --> 00:36:37,662
[Joel] Yeah, yeah, I got to pick up
a thing of wax worms.

933
00:36:37,762 --> 00:36:39,364
I don't think he'll give us
any trouble, Josh.

934
00:36:39,431 --> 00:36:40,632
[Crow mumbling] Josh.

935
00:36:40,699 --> 00:36:43,068
That's what Fremont said
about Stonewall Jackson.

936
00:36:43,668 --> 00:36:45,370
-[Servo] Walked right into that.
-I think you're right.

937
00:36:45,437 --> 00:36:46,771
I know I'm right.

938
00:36:47,005 --> 00:36:51,176
Maybe I'd better find out
what his business is right now.

939
00:36:51,242 --> 00:36:52,944
You be careful, Miss Rose.

940
00:36:53,011 --> 00:36:54,646
He won't even know I'm following him.

941
00:36:56,147 --> 00:36:57,849
[Joel] Hey, she's following me.

942
00:36:57,916 --> 00:36:58,783
[Crow with feminine voice] Oh, shoot.

943
00:37:00,985 --> 00:37:03,555
[Servo] It's going to be a bad day.
We're even out of TP.

944
00:37:08,026 --> 00:37:09,060
[Joel] A strange feller.

945
00:37:10,261 --> 00:37:12,564
[Servo] Well, one more trip
to the buffet.

946
00:37:16,201 --> 00:37:17,836
[Crow] Cute outdoor cafe.

947
00:37:19,971 --> 00:37:22,006
[Joel] Yeah, she needs
operatives, all right.

948
00:37:23,241 --> 00:37:25,110
[Crow] What the--?
How'd he get there?

949
00:37:25,176 --> 00:37:26,177
[Servo] Wait a minute.

950
00:37:30,582 --> 00:37:31,649
[Servo scoffs]

951
00:37:35,019 --> 00:37:37,756
[Crow] Do I order
from you, ma'am? Uh, ma-- Oh.

952
00:37:40,625 --> 00:37:42,794
[Joel] That's two guys
in a horse costume.

953
00:37:42,861 --> 00:37:44,496
[bots laugh]

954
00:37:45,997 --> 00:37:47,732
[Crow] Doesn't 'marshal'
have two Ls in it?

955
00:37:47,799 --> 00:37:49,134
-[Servo] Well, it's either.
-[Crow] Oh.

956
00:37:49,200 --> 00:37:50,401
[Crow] Well, it should have
two Ls, it looks better.

957
00:37:50,468 --> 00:37:51,603
[Servo whispers] It's either.

958
00:37:52,003 --> 00:37:54,939
[Servo] ♪ Dennis Moore, Dennis Moore
Riding through the night ♪

959
00:37:55,006 --> 00:37:56,775
<i>♪ Dum, dum dum, dum, dum, dum ♪</i>

960
00:37:56,841 --> 00:37:58,843
[Joel] Hey, cameraman,
crank a little faster.

961
00:37:58,910 --> 00:37:59,944
[Crow giggles]

962
00:38:00,578 --> 00:38:02,647
[Servo] She does like me. Heh.

963
00:38:02,714 --> 00:38:04,682
[Crow makes siren noise]

964
00:38:04,749 --> 00:38:07,652
[Joel] Oh boy, I hope there's
no black ice on their route.

965
00:38:09,654 --> 00:38:11,089
[Crow] Well, I think I'll stop
by the tennis court

966
00:38:11,156 --> 00:38:12,190
on the way home.

967
00:38:16,194 --> 00:38:19,931
[Joel] ♪ Marvel the Mustang
<i>She's almost for real ♪</i>

968
00:38:26,371 --> 00:38:29,107
[Crow] He likes to get
way out of town to pee.

969
00:38:30,942 --> 00:38:33,344
[Servo] What do you--
It's Jack Nicholson's place.

970
00:38:39,384 --> 00:38:41,619
[Joel] Hey, you forgot
your Snack Pack.

971
00:38:44,155 --> 00:38:46,491
You knew I was
following you all the time.

972
00:38:46,558 --> 00:38:47,592
[Crow] So did everyone else
in the county.

973
00:38:47,659 --> 00:38:49,327
Now that you caught me,
what do you want?

974
00:38:49,394 --> 00:38:50,628
[Joel] You're it.

975
00:38:50,695 --> 00:38:52,530
Well, that's a very good question.

976
00:38:53,832 --> 00:38:55,567
Why don't you get down,
take a load off your horse?

977
00:38:56,167 --> 00:38:57,936
[Crow] Oh, and what's
that supposed to mean?

978
00:38:58,002 --> 00:38:59,904
How's your business coming along?

979
00:38:59,971 --> 00:39:02,307
[Joel] Recession hit me
like everyone else.

980
00:39:02,373 --> 00:39:04,475
What were you seeing
Canby Judd about?

981
00:39:04,542 --> 00:39:06,477
Something that's still private.

982
00:39:07,812 --> 00:39:10,415
You don't have many answers
to my questions, do you?

983
00:39:11,082 --> 00:39:12,851
You don't ask the right questions.

984
00:39:13,251 --> 00:39:15,420
[Servo] Oh, boy,
they're bantering again.

985
00:39:18,556 --> 00:39:19,424
[Joel] Excuse me.

986
00:39:19,490 --> 00:39:22,627
When... When you were
in Tombstone, did you...

987
00:39:22,694 --> 00:39:23,628
[Crow] Eat much pizza?

988
00:39:23,695 --> 00:39:25,196
...did you ever run across Sam Bass?

989
00:39:25,930 --> 00:39:27,498
Sure. Sam and me are old friends.

990
00:39:27,565 --> 00:39:29,234
We used to work together.

991
00:39:30,101 --> 00:39:31,336
Well, he's a lawman now.

992
00:39:31,736 --> 00:39:32,604
As a matter of fact,

993
00:39:32,670 --> 00:39:34,839
he'll be here Saturday
to take over my job.

994
00:39:35,974 --> 00:39:37,675
Morning, noon, or night?

995
00:39:37,742 --> 00:39:40,612
[chuckling]
What difference does that make?

996
00:39:40,678 --> 00:39:42,213
[Joel] Hey, this is moving
too fast for me.

997
00:39:42,280 --> 00:39:43,314
Some, I guess.

998
00:39:43,715 --> 00:39:45,884
-[Servo with high-pitched voice] Hi.
-So, ol' Sam's crossed over, huh?

999
00:39:45,950 --> 00:39:47,018
[Crow] Wearin' dresses and stuff.

1000
00:39:47,085 --> 00:39:48,953
Well, he'll come back. We all do.

1001
00:39:49,621 --> 00:39:52,056
I spent a couple of months
playing sheriff myself.

1002
00:39:52,590 --> 00:39:53,691
How'd you make out?

1003
00:39:54,325 --> 00:39:56,494
Plenty of action but the pay was lousy.

1004
00:39:56,561 --> 00:39:57,595
[chuckling]

1005
00:39:57,762 --> 00:39:59,530
Then why is it all the worst gunslingers

1006
00:39:59,597 --> 00:40:00,932
take up law work?

1007
00:40:00,999 --> 00:40:03,301
Look at Wyatt Earp,
Bat Masterson, King Fisher.

1008
00:40:03,368 --> 00:40:04,369
[Joel] Yeah, good shows.

1009
00:40:04,435 --> 00:40:06,604
Each one of them
is a coldblooded killer.

1010
00:40:06,671 --> 00:40:08,273
You answered that yourself.

1011
00:40:08,940 --> 00:40:11,342
For me, crime is just a way to get rich.

1012
00:40:11,709 --> 00:40:12,844
Those other fellows like to kill,

1013
00:40:12,911 --> 00:40:15,246
and there's more chance when it's legal,

1014
00:40:15,313 --> 00:40:17,448
like a license for murder.

1015
00:40:17,515 --> 00:40:19,150
[Servo] That is so true!

1016
00:40:19,350 --> 00:40:20,718
Why don't you apply for one?

1017
00:40:20,785 --> 00:40:22,320
[Joel] No, I don't have
very good references.

1018
00:40:22,387 --> 00:40:23,554
I'll make you a deal.

1019
00:40:24,389 --> 00:40:26,791
I won't try to make you a bad woman

1020
00:40:26,858 --> 00:40:28,726
if you stop trying
to make me a good man.

1021
00:40:28,793 --> 00:40:30,128
[Servo] It's a country song, isn't it?

1022
00:40:31,429 --> 00:40:32,397
You're not bad...

1023
00:40:32,463 --> 00:40:33,598
[Crow] You're just drawn that way.

1024
00:40:33,665 --> 00:40:34,899
...you're just no good.

1025
00:40:34,966 --> 00:40:36,134
[Joel] Is that bad?

1026
00:40:36,200 --> 00:40:39,070
If I'm no good, I might as well
take advantage of it.

1027
00:40:39,137 --> 00:40:41,005
[Servo] Sorry, my wooden hip.

1028
00:40:43,474 --> 00:40:45,944
-No thanks.
-[Joel] I don't think out, soul brother.

1029
00:40:47,412 --> 00:40:48,780
[Servo] Maybe just a little.

1030
00:40:48,846 --> 00:40:49,914
-[Joel] Does this mean that they--?
-[Servo moaning]

1031
00:40:49,981 --> 00:40:52,350
[Joel] Because they were going to--?
And then they--?

1032
00:40:56,921 --> 00:40:59,123
[Servo as horse] Oh, pull my back.
Oh, pull my back.

1033
00:41:00,458 --> 00:41:01,960
[Crow] Hi, Wormy.

1034
00:41:02,026 --> 00:41:04,128
Didn't I leave you back
at the Red Dog?

1035
00:41:04,195 --> 00:41:05,897
Erica sent me after you.

1036
00:41:05,964 --> 00:41:07,765
She thinks she shortchanged you.

1037
00:41:07,832 --> 00:41:10,034
Shortchanged? By how much?

1038
00:41:10,101 --> 00:41:10,969
Just this.

1039
00:41:11,970 --> 00:41:13,705
-[Servo] Oh, thanks.
-[Crow] Ooh.

1040
00:41:13,771 --> 00:41:16,174
[Servo] Come on, honey, you're not
the Sheriff of the world.

1041
00:41:16,240 --> 00:41:17,642
Instead of doing my job, I'm out here

1042
00:41:17,709 --> 00:41:19,844
disgracing Scott's memory
and it's all your fault.

1043
00:41:19,911 --> 00:41:21,713
Nothing we both do is all my fault.

1044
00:41:21,779 --> 00:41:23,815
[Joel] Tracy and Hepburn
riding the range.

1045
00:41:26,484 --> 00:41:29,921
Wow, this is great,
kind of got a Pony Express,

1046
00:41:29,988 --> 00:41:32,623
kind of Gypsy Express thing.

1047
00:41:32,690 --> 00:41:35,760
Whoa! Stand back, the bullion,

1048
00:41:35,827 --> 00:41:38,296
you may be interfering
with this daring horseback rider

1049
00:41:38,363 --> 00:41:39,864
of the Pony Express,

1050
00:41:39,931 --> 00:41:42,467
carrying mail from
the Satellite of Love to the...

1051
00:41:42,533 --> 00:41:44,569
-Whoa, girl. Satellite of Love.

1052
00:41:44,635 --> 00:41:47,972
-Whoa, girl.
-Make haste, man! Be gone, off with you!

1053
00:41:48,106 --> 00:41:50,274
-[Servo] Godspeed!
-[Crow] Oh, Concord!

1054
00:41:50,341 --> 00:41:51,843
[Crow] Owie, owie.
Owie, owie. Owie, owie.

1055
00:41:51,909 --> 00:41:55,046
There goes a brave seller
and his brave horse.

1056
00:41:55,113 --> 00:41:56,047
Oh, by the way, Joel,

1057
00:41:56,114 --> 00:41:57,315
I am sending you
a very important message.

1058
00:41:57,382 --> 00:41:58,649
-OK.
-[Crow] Owie, owie. Owie, owie...

1059
00:41:58,816 --> 00:42:01,552
I just hope to God
it gets to you in time.

1060
00:42:01,619 --> 00:42:05,423
Servo, I'm standing
right here, what is the point?

1061
00:42:05,490 --> 00:42:07,358
-That is, Joel. Just play along!
-[Crow] Owie, owie. Owie, owie...

1062
00:42:07,425 --> 00:42:09,894
[Crow] Whoa, Gypsy,
watch out for that--

1063
00:42:09,961 --> 00:42:11,662
[crash]

1064
00:42:11,729 --> 00:42:12,697
Ow.

1065
00:42:12,897 --> 00:42:16,100
So, what did you write to me
in that letter?

1066
00:42:16,167 --> 00:42:17,835
Oh, that I wanted a peanut
butter and dijonaisse sandwich

1067
00:42:17,902 --> 00:42:19,504
and a Snapple for lunch.

1068
00:42:19,570 --> 00:42:23,007
-[Gypsy neighing]
-[Crow] Whoa. Whoa. Whoa, girl.

1069
00:42:23,074 --> 00:42:25,476
Oh, Crow, you are a lot heavier
than you appear to be.

1070
00:42:26,644 --> 00:42:28,880
You are Joel Robinstone?

1071
00:42:28,946 --> 00:42:32,583
That's Joel Robinson, yes.
And this is for me, I am mad.

1072
00:42:32,650 --> 00:42:34,886
-OK, let's see here.
-[Servo] Give me a little kiss here.

1073
00:42:34,952 --> 00:42:37,288
-Uh, "Dear Joel..."
-[Crow] Easy, girl.

1074
00:42:37,355 --> 00:42:41,659
"Dear Joel, how are you?
I'm fine, I want a something something

1075
00:42:41,726 --> 00:42:43,528
and a Snapple for lunch.

1076
00:42:43,594 --> 00:42:45,129
Yours very truly, Servo."

1077
00:42:45,196 --> 00:42:46,531
OK, I'm going to have
to respond to this.

1078
00:42:46,597 --> 00:42:48,433
Peanut butter and dijonaisse sandwich,
Joel, it's very simple.

1079
00:42:48,499 --> 00:42:50,134
Yeah, could you turn around?
Let me just write this down.

1080
00:42:50,201 --> 00:42:53,738
"OK, Dear Servo, I'm in receipt

1081
00:42:53,805 --> 00:42:55,640
"of your correspondence
regarding lunch

1082
00:42:55,706 --> 00:42:57,909
"and I regret to inform you
that I cannot read

1083
00:42:57,975 --> 00:43:02,713
"the two words you wrote between
'I want a' and 'a Snapple.'

1084
00:43:02,780 --> 00:43:05,416
"Please respond at your convenience
or before lunch.

1085
00:43:05,483 --> 00:43:07,018
Regards, Joel."

1086
00:43:07,085 --> 00:43:08,419
Peanut butter
and dijonaisse sandwich.

1087
00:43:08,486 --> 00:43:10,421
-It's not that difficult.
-Oh, for Christ's sake.

1088
00:43:10,488 --> 00:43:12,423
This is going to take forever.
I'm so hungry.

1089
00:43:12,490 --> 00:43:14,192
-[Gypsy neighing]
-[Crow] Whoa! Whoa!

1090
00:43:16,828 --> 00:43:18,663
Well, you know,
those kids don't even know

1091
00:43:18,729 --> 00:43:20,932
that the shortest distance
between two points

1092
00:43:20,998 --> 00:43:22,633
-is a straight line.
-[Crow] Owie, owie. Owie, owie...

1093
00:43:22,700 --> 00:43:24,735
What could be taking them so long?

1094
00:43:24,802 --> 00:43:26,904
-[Gypsy neighing]
-[Crow] Whoa! Whoa!

1095
00:43:28,940 --> 00:43:31,909
-[alarm buzzing]
-[Servo] Whoa, we got movie time!

1096
00:43:40,585 --> 00:43:41,752
[Joel] That's a lot of sandwich.

1097
00:43:43,754 --> 00:43:45,523
[Servo] Sir, you can't park here.

1098
00:43:47,525 --> 00:43:48,626
Zebelon Tabb.

1099
00:43:50,027 --> 00:43:51,796
Third businessman
to leave Oracle this week.

1100
00:43:51,863 --> 00:43:52,897
[Joel] Huh.

1101
00:43:56,534 --> 00:43:59,070
[Servo] Hey, how did I end up
back at--? Oh, Poopy.

1102
00:44:02,874 --> 00:44:05,776
[Crow] Oh, now we're back
to June 1st.

1103
00:44:07,845 --> 00:44:10,348
[Servo] Pa, Pa, I'm seeing
some trouble in town.

1104
00:44:10,414 --> 00:44:13,484
[piano music playing within]

1105
00:44:14,619 --> 00:44:16,354
[Crow] Jack Ruby on piano.

1106
00:44:16,420 --> 00:44:18,055
Hold it. That was lousy.

1107
00:44:18,122 --> 00:44:19,590
You've gotta get more leg into it.

1108
00:44:19,657 --> 00:44:22,226
Oh, why bother? We've gotta be
out of town by tomorrow night.

1109
00:44:22,293 --> 00:44:24,128
Forget it. Go take a bath.

1110
00:44:24,195 --> 00:44:25,730
You too. Work up a quick head.

1111
00:44:25,796 --> 00:44:28,499
[Joel] All right, I'll go change
into my leotard.

1112
00:44:30,334 --> 00:44:31,569
Gotta talk to you.

1113
00:44:31,636 --> 00:44:33,804
-Did you get the money?
-Yeah, yeah. Every penny.

1114
00:44:33,871 --> 00:44:34,839
Hand it over.

1115
00:44:38,109 --> 00:44:40,578
-What's the matter?
-[Crow] I killed a guy and I wet him.

1116
00:44:40,645 --> 00:44:41,646
Something went wrong.

1117
00:44:41,746 --> 00:44:44,448
No, no. I didn't have time
<i>to get rid of the body.</i>

1118
00:44:44,549 --> 00:44:45,616
<i>Where is it?</i>

1119
00:44:46,350 --> 00:44:48,052
Cane Miro and the lady marshal have it.

1120
00:44:48,119 --> 00:44:49,120
[Erica] What?

1121
00:44:49,187 --> 00:44:50,788
<i>They're bringin' it into town.</i>

1122
00:44:52,356 --> 00:44:53,824
<i>Cane and Rose?</i>

1123
00:44:53,891 --> 00:44:54,759
[Jake] That's right.

1124
00:44:54,825 --> 00:44:57,228
[Servo in feminine voice]
So crazy, it just might work.

1125
00:44:57,295 --> 00:44:58,829
<i>Cane and Rose.</i>

1126
00:44:58,896 --> 00:45:00,965
[Joel] This fall on NBC,
<i>Cane and Rose...</i>

1127
00:45:02,900 --> 00:45:05,102
[Servo] Oh, neat!
Dark specter in basic black.

1128
00:45:09,340 --> 00:45:11,075
<i>[woman] Rose,</i>
<i>I've got to talk to you.</i>

1129
00:45:11,142 --> 00:45:14,378
[Joel] It's about your yard,
the junk cars, the garbage... Oh.

1130
00:45:16,447 --> 00:45:17,915
[knocking on door]

1131
00:45:17,982 --> 00:45:20,985
[Joel] Ah. Just about to give
myself a sponge bath.

1132
00:45:25,389 --> 00:45:27,658
[Crow] But-- Doors don't open
like that, there's an--

1133
00:45:27,725 --> 00:45:29,360
-He's in the hall.
-[Servo laughs]

1134
00:45:29,427 --> 00:45:30,695
<i>You crazy, coming up here?</i>

1135
00:45:30,761 --> 00:45:31,896
[Joel] In my hallway.

1136
00:45:34,699 --> 00:45:35,533
[Servo] Well, I'll just talk to you
about it later then.

1137
00:45:35,600 --> 00:45:37,368
<i>Miro aims to kill Gideon.</i>

1138
00:45:37,435 --> 00:45:38,903
<i>I know that, honey.</i>

1139
00:45:38,970 --> 00:45:41,372
-Where is your husband?
-Erica Page hid him out in the woods.

1140
00:45:41,639 --> 00:45:42,740
[Crow] He might
get ticks or something.

1141
00:45:42,807 --> 00:45:43,941
<i>Erica's a busy girl.</i>

1142
00:45:44,008 --> 00:45:45,910
[Joel] What, with her volunteer
work and everything.

1143
00:45:45,977 --> 00:45:48,879
Just what is it that Cane
<i>has got against the mayor?</i>

1144
00:45:49,046 --> 00:45:50,047
<i>I don't know.</i>

1145
00:45:50,114 --> 00:45:51,882
<i>The one story he's never told me.</i>

1146
00:45:52,083 --> 00:45:53,517
<i>Now I wish he had.</i>

1147
00:45:53,584 --> 00:45:54,619
<i>Well, one thing's sure.</i>

1148
00:45:54,685 --> 00:45:57,321
<i>He's got to be back in town</i>
<i>by Saturday to read that letter.</i>

1149
00:45:57,388 --> 00:45:59,123
<i>Yeah, he's afraid of that, too.</i>

1150
00:45:59,190 --> 00:46:01,726
Afraid the town'll dry up
<i>and blow out from under him.</i>

1151
00:46:01,792 --> 00:46:03,294
[Servo] Like me.

1152
00:46:03,361 --> 00:46:05,529
<i>Erica Page is no welfare worker.</i>

1153
00:46:06,063 --> 00:46:07,632
<i>Why's she taking such an interest?</i>

1154
00:46:08,132 --> 00:46:10,368
[Crow] Hey, she's the first woman
with her own eyebrows.

1155
00:46:10,434 --> 00:46:14,338
Land scheme. Legal, of course.
Gideon does everything legal.

1156
00:46:15,573 --> 00:46:17,608
<i>Have they been involved</i>
<i>with Canby Judd?</i>

1157
00:46:17,708 --> 00:46:19,076
I believe so.

1158
00:46:19,243 --> 00:46:21,545
I know Mr. Judd is thinking
of leaving Oracle.

1159
00:46:22,380 --> 00:46:24,081
<i>Where has Erica hidden your husband?</i>

1160
00:46:24,315 --> 00:46:26,484
He's at the old Wilson place
<i>in Greasewood Canyon.</i>

1161
00:46:26,550 --> 00:46:27,551
[all three] Ew!

1162
00:46:27,618 --> 00:46:28,886
<i>Could you go out and see him?</i>

1163
00:46:29,887 --> 00:46:31,155
<i>I'll go first thing in the morning.</i>

1164
00:46:31,222 --> 00:46:32,990
<i>Oh, I'd appreciate that.</i>

1165
00:46:33,057 --> 00:46:35,493
The sooner he knows
<i>you're looking after him, the better.</i>

1166
00:46:35,559 --> 00:46:36,861
[Joel] Hey, chocolate gorilla foot.

1167
00:46:36,927 --> 00:46:38,029
[Crow] Huh, what do you know.

1168
00:46:40,031 --> 00:46:43,200
I'd go tonight, but there's something
I've got to attend to first.

1169
00:46:43,367 --> 00:46:44,702
Thanks very much, Rose. I...

1170
00:46:44,769 --> 00:46:47,104
I can't tell you
<i>how much this means to me.</i>

1171
00:46:47,171 --> 00:46:50,041
And to think we laughed
at the notion of you wearin' Scott's star.

1172
00:46:50,107 --> 00:46:51,208
[Joel laughs]

1173
00:46:51,275 --> 00:46:53,611
[Crow] Hey, a simple
handshake will do.

1174
00:46:54,278 --> 00:46:55,813
[Joel] I think she touched
my handles.

1175
00:46:57,815 --> 00:47:00,518
[Servo] Meanwhile,
back at the love shack.

1176
00:47:01,752 --> 00:47:03,788
[Crow] What time is it?

1177
00:47:04,388 --> 00:47:05,823
You're getting careless.

1178
00:47:06,123 --> 00:47:07,825
[Joel] Yeah, sorry, I've been
on the trail a long time.

1179
00:47:07,892 --> 00:47:10,961
Not as careless as your
little halfwit killer, Jake.

1180
00:47:11,128 --> 00:47:13,030
I recognize your subtle touch.

1181
00:47:13,664 --> 00:47:15,132
You don't miss much, do you?

1182
00:47:16,067 --> 00:47:17,668
You wanna watch yourself, though.

1183
00:47:18,269 --> 00:47:20,938
Rose says there's been other
similar incidents around here.

1184
00:47:22,306 --> 00:47:23,908
[Servo] I hate it when
there are similar incidents.

1185
00:47:23,974 --> 00:47:25,109
What was that for?

1186
00:47:25,176 --> 00:47:27,278
So, you admit being with her
this afternoon?

1187
00:47:28,979 --> 00:47:31,716
-Sure, why not?
-[Joel with dopey voice] Oh, it's fun.

1188
00:47:32,016 --> 00:47:34,318
-I've made up my mind.
-[Crow] I'm going to be an upholsterer.

1189
00:47:34,385 --> 00:47:35,986
I want her dead tomorrow.

1190
00:47:36,454 --> 00:47:37,755
I told you, no changes.

1191
00:47:37,822 --> 00:47:39,023
[Servo] Now, get out of my hall.

1192
00:47:43,694 --> 00:47:45,529
Maybe I won't need you at all.

1193
00:47:48,399 --> 00:47:50,701
[Joel] Wait a minute, she's in
my room now. Where do I go?

1194
00:47:55,306 --> 00:47:56,340
Waiting in ambush?

1195
00:47:56,407 --> 00:47:57,708
[Crow] No, I'm wearing ambush.

1196
00:47:57,775 --> 00:47:59,210
I don't think I have to do that.

1197
00:48:00,644 --> 00:48:02,113
Are the girls ready to leave?

1198
00:48:02,380 --> 00:48:04,515
You said Friday.
This is only Tuesday night.

1199
00:48:05,383 --> 00:48:06,550
Just a reminder.

1200
00:48:07,118 --> 00:48:08,552
Well, thank you.

1201
00:48:09,086 --> 00:48:11,389
Now that I've been reminded,
may I go on to the Red Dog?

1202
00:48:12,823 --> 00:48:14,692
You may go to the red devil,
as far as I'm concerned.

1203
00:48:14,759 --> 00:48:17,328
With Red Buttons to watch<i> Red Dwarf.</i>

1204
00:48:18,496 --> 00:48:20,331
[Crow] Oh, and this town
ain't big enough for the...

1205
00:48:20,398 --> 00:48:21,732
Oh, you know the rest.

1206
00:48:23,300 --> 00:48:25,536
[Servo] Well, I feel good
after damning someone to hell.

1207
00:48:25,603 --> 00:48:27,505
I'm going to rustle me up
some Hormel Chili.

1208
00:48:29,240 --> 00:48:32,042
Say, Deputy, you shoulda seen
what I said to that Erica girl.

1209
00:48:32,109 --> 00:48:33,077
[knocking on door]

1210
00:48:34,111 --> 00:48:35,946
-Come in.
-[Joel] Or out.

1211
00:48:36,414 --> 00:48:37,348
[door opens]

1212
00:48:38,482 --> 00:48:39,717
[Crow] Why is all your stuff
in the hallway?

1213
00:48:39,784 --> 00:48:42,286
-Are you alone?
-Almost never, it looks like.

1214
00:48:42,353 --> 00:48:44,321
-[Servo] And this is hallway here.
-Come on in.

1215
00:48:44,388 --> 00:48:46,023
People'll think you're
collecting for the poor.

1216
00:48:47,425 --> 00:48:48,526
In a way I guess I am.

1217
00:48:48,592 --> 00:48:50,795
[Joel] It's a walkathon.
You want to sponsor me?

1218
00:48:50,861 --> 00:48:51,729
Sit down.

1219
00:48:53,864 --> 00:48:55,032
Picture of yourself?

1220
00:48:56,000 --> 00:48:57,201
Yeah, an old one.

1221
00:48:57,268 --> 00:48:58,836
[Servo] Reason I have
my pants off is...

1222
00:48:58,903 --> 00:49:00,771
This Rebel officer, isn't it...?

1223
00:49:00,971 --> 00:49:02,373
Captain Gideon Polk.

1224
00:49:02,440 --> 00:49:03,607
[Joel] Oh, the Bible guy?

1225
00:49:05,709 --> 00:49:08,479
-His wife says you want to kill him.
-[Servo] No, no, kiss him.

1226
00:49:08,546 --> 00:49:10,681
I've been looking for him
since 1865 to kill him.

1227
00:49:10,748 --> 00:49:12,750
-[Joel] A hundred years?
-Why?

1228
00:49:12,817 --> 00:49:14,084
Because he lost us the war.

1229
00:49:14,151 --> 00:49:15,386
Oh, Cane, don't be ridiculous.

1230
00:49:15,453 --> 00:49:17,288
As far as I'm concerned, he did.

1231
00:49:18,422 --> 00:49:19,490
He killed my four brothers.

1232
00:49:19,557 --> 00:49:21,392
-[Crow] And my forefathers.
-What?

1233
00:49:21,892 --> 00:49:23,394
Oh, he didn't murder them outright.

1234
00:49:23,461 --> 00:49:25,329
He just fed them to the Yankees.

1235
00:49:25,396 --> 00:49:27,298
[Joel] With a choice
of salad, soup, or juice.

1236
00:49:27,364 --> 00:49:28,232
What happened?

1237
00:49:29,400 --> 00:49:31,702
Like the man says, it's a long story.

1238
00:49:31,769 --> 00:49:32,970
[Crow] Do you have any sisters?

1239
00:49:33,604 --> 00:49:34,738
I've got nothing to do.

1240
00:49:37,541 --> 00:49:39,443
Are you familiar with
the Battle of Lookout Mountain?

1241
00:49:39,510 --> 00:49:40,711
[Servo] That's one
of my favorite battles.

1242
00:49:40,778 --> 00:49:41,846
Only what I learned in school.

1243
00:49:44,648 --> 00:49:46,083
-[Joel] Oh, boy.
-[Crow] Here we go.

1244
00:49:46,150 --> 00:49:47,885
{\an8}My brothers and I
were in an artillery battery

1245
00:49:47,952 --> 00:49:49,587
{\an8}commanded by Captain Polk.

1246
00:49:50,621 --> 00:49:52,857
{\an8}Lookout Mountain was where
we had the Yankees under siege.

1247
00:49:52,923 --> 00:49:54,225
{\an8}[Joel] With Steven Seagal.

1248
00:49:54,291 --> 00:49:55,659
{\an8}They had to get us off those ridges

1249
00:49:55,726 --> 00:49:56,760
{\an8}but they couldn't.

1250
00:49:56,861 --> 00:49:57,995
{\an8}-But they did.
-[Servo] But they couldn't.

1251
00:49:58,062 --> 00:49:59,763
Our position was impregnable.

1252
00:49:59,830 --> 00:50:00,898
[Crow] You can't say that.

1253
00:50:01,031 --> 00:50:03,167
The only weak line
was at the foot of the ridge.

1254
00:50:03,234 --> 00:50:04,401
[Joel] Sing out, brother.

1255
00:50:04,468 --> 00:50:06,670
Polk's battery was
in a beautiful position halfway down.

1256
00:50:06,737 --> 00:50:08,038
[Joel] Righteous.

1257
00:50:08,105 --> 00:50:09,640
The Yankees charged.

1258
00:50:09,707 --> 00:50:11,175
Grant ordered them to take
only the trench

1259
00:50:11,242 --> 00:50:12,943
-at the edge of the ridge.
-[Joel] Testify.

1260
00:50:13,077 --> 00:50:15,379
We had 'em cold and we cut 'em down,

1261
00:50:15,446 --> 00:50:16,380
but they massed again

1262
00:50:16,447 --> 00:50:17,781
and came out again over their own dead.

1263
00:50:17,848 --> 00:50:18,682
[Joel] Take it home.

1264
00:50:18,749 --> 00:50:20,918
A shell exploded inside
the body of a Yankee officer

1265
00:50:20,985 --> 00:50:21,819
right in front of us.

1266
00:50:21,886 --> 00:50:23,020
[Servo with feminine voice]
I had to ask.

1267
00:50:23,087 --> 00:50:24,822
Polk saw it and ran.

1268
00:50:25,155 --> 00:50:27,057
At the height of our victory, he ran.

1269
00:50:28,192 --> 00:50:30,060
My brothers and a few of us
stuck with our guns

1270
00:50:30,127 --> 00:50:33,130
but the fever caught,
and the whole center broke.

1271
00:50:33,197 --> 00:50:34,031
It was the end of the battle

1272
00:50:34,098 --> 00:50:37,601
and it meant...the end of the war.

1273
00:50:37,668 --> 00:50:39,336
[Servo] I'm just hitting
the highlights here.

1274
00:50:39,870 --> 00:50:43,040
My brothers were killed
and I was captured.

1275
00:50:43,107 --> 00:50:44,642
-[Servo] Bummer.
-[Crow] Live and learn.

1276
00:50:44,708 --> 00:50:45,943
I don't quite understand.

1277
00:50:46,010 --> 00:50:47,811
-[Joel] Who won?
-It's very simple.

1278
00:50:48,245 --> 00:50:49,346
If we hadn't lost Lookout Mountain,

1279
00:50:49,413 --> 00:50:50,881
there would've been an armistice.

1280
00:50:51,549 --> 00:50:53,050
The Confederacy would still be alive.

1281
00:50:53,117 --> 00:50:54,418
And the Vikings would have
finally captured

1282
00:50:54,485 --> 00:50:55,953
a Super Bowl title.

1283
00:50:56,754 --> 00:50:59,156
One man, one stinking coward.

1284
00:50:59,857 --> 00:51:01,191
[Servo] You're not
buying this, are you?

1285
00:51:02,560 --> 00:51:03,727
I'm sorry.

1286
00:51:03,794 --> 00:51:05,296
[Joel] Well, at least
you had brothers.

1287
00:51:05,362 --> 00:51:07,431
Guess I was beginning
to live it all over again.

1288
00:51:10,134 --> 00:51:12,169
-Don't apologize.
-[Joel] I'm sorry.

1289
00:51:12,436 --> 00:51:14,004
I know how you feel about it.

1290
00:51:14,071 --> 00:51:15,606
[Crow] Do you have
any snacks or anything?

1291
00:51:15,673 --> 00:51:18,542
But you're wrong. You're dead wrong.

1292
00:51:19,109 --> 00:51:20,711
You can't blame the loss of a war

1293
00:51:20,778 --> 00:51:22,413
on one low-ranking officer.

1294
00:51:22,479 --> 00:51:23,714
[Joel] I can't?

1295
00:51:23,781 --> 00:51:24,915
You weren't there.

1296
00:51:25,449 --> 00:51:26,750
That doesn't make any difference.

1297
00:51:27,685 --> 00:51:28,986
Don't you think the remembrance of this

1298
00:51:29,053 --> 00:51:31,488
has made him pay for it
over and over again?

1299
00:51:31,956 --> 00:51:33,691
A million men died for nothing.

1300
00:51:33,757 --> 00:51:35,759
Only one bore a green beret.

1301
00:51:35,826 --> 00:51:38,228
But as I said before,
they all die sooner or later.

1302
00:51:38,295 --> 00:51:39,263
[Crow] When did he say that?

1303
00:51:39,330 --> 00:51:40,965
And sooner or later, everyone runs...

1304
00:51:41,031 --> 00:51:42,266
[Joel] Especially Wilma Rudolph.

1305
00:51:42,333 --> 00:51:43,534
-[Servo] Mmm.
-...at least once.

1306
00:51:44,301 --> 00:51:45,736
Forget it.

1307
00:51:45,803 --> 00:51:47,438
[Servo] Well, our hour's almost up here.

1308
00:51:47,504 --> 00:51:49,273
Did you want to schedule next week?

1309
00:51:51,909 --> 00:51:53,177
You'll leave him alone?

1310
00:51:53,844 --> 00:51:55,579
-Sure.
-[Joel] I'm not that mad.

1311
00:51:55,646 --> 00:51:57,948
[Servo] Easiest vendetta in the West.

1312
00:51:58,983 --> 00:52:00,851
[Joel] Now, she's in my room again.

1313
00:52:00,918 --> 00:52:02,286
What am I gonna do?

1314
00:52:03,921 --> 00:52:05,756
Hold it. Who is it?

1315
00:52:06,757 --> 00:52:08,092
Beauregard and Sapp.

1316
00:52:08,158 --> 00:52:09,226
[Servo] They're cops.

1317
00:52:10,127 --> 00:52:11,061
Sorry, Rose.

1318
00:52:12,096 --> 00:52:13,564
I'm gettin' a little jumpy.

1319
00:52:13,631 --> 00:52:15,165
-[Servo] Which one's Beauregard?
-Felicity send you?

1320
00:52:15,232 --> 00:52:17,301
How about some Crystal Light,
just made a batch.

1321
00:52:17,368 --> 00:52:20,204
She told me you were here.
I just came to tell you you were safe.

1322
00:52:20,904 --> 00:52:22,139
You mean, Cane Miro's gone?

1323
00:52:22,206 --> 00:52:24,241
Well, no, he's not gone,
but I gave him until Saturday

1324
00:52:24,308 --> 00:52:26,243
to finish his business and ride.

1325
00:52:26,310 --> 00:52:29,079
Oh, so that's what Erica meant.

1326
00:52:29,146 --> 00:52:31,415
-[Crow] They're stuck in a subplot.
-Erica?

1327
00:52:31,482 --> 00:52:32,549
Yeah, she said he'd be gone

1328
00:52:32,616 --> 00:52:34,218
after that railroad letter arrived.

1329
00:52:35,119 --> 00:52:37,021
What's Erica got to do with Cane?

1330
00:52:37,087 --> 00:52:38,389
She didn't say,

1331
00:52:38,455 --> 00:52:40,891
but it can't be for a date
for Sunday school.

1332
00:52:41,892 --> 00:52:44,695
[Servo] Mmm, I have to go over here
and think about this.

1333
00:52:44,762 --> 00:52:45,863
This one is deep.

1334
00:52:46,964 --> 00:52:48,766
Everything seems to add up to Saturday...

1335
00:52:49,867 --> 00:52:53,303
Railroad letter, Sam Bass,
my ultimatum to Cane...

1336
00:52:53,370 --> 00:52:55,439
-[Joel] The fishing opener.
-And now Erica.

1337
00:52:57,408 --> 00:52:58,275
Well, if she's not careful,

1338
00:52:58,342 --> 00:53:00,344
she's gonna connive herself
right into one of my cells.

1339
00:53:00,411 --> 00:53:01,912
[Servo] Careful, that's
the main beam there.

1340
00:53:01,979 --> 00:53:03,414
Well, I just want to be sure
you're comfortable.

1341
00:53:03,480 --> 00:53:04,415
Have you got everything you need?

1342
00:53:04,481 --> 00:53:06,850
Eh, I could use a few troops of cavalry.

1343
00:53:06,917 --> 00:53:09,253
-[Crow] Ha, I don't get it.
-For now, Josh and I will have to do.

1344
00:53:09,319 --> 00:53:11,155
I'll tell Felicity that you're here.

1345
00:53:11,221 --> 00:53:13,057
Are you sure he can't find me here?

1346
00:53:13,791 --> 00:53:15,693
[Rose] He'd never find you
in a million years.

1347
00:53:15,759 --> 00:53:18,195
[Joel] Apparently they haven't
invented peripheral vision.

1348
00:53:18,262 --> 00:53:19,830
Well, goodbye, Rose.

1349
00:53:19,897 --> 00:53:20,764
I'll see you on Saturday.

1350
00:53:21,699 --> 00:53:22,599
Come on, boy.

1351
00:53:22,666 --> 00:53:26,637
[Servo] Guests of Beverly Garland
stay as the Beverly Garland Hotel.

1352
00:53:27,905 --> 00:53:29,807
[Joel] I like that sheriff, I do.

1353
00:53:31,375 --> 00:53:32,943
[Servo]<i> ♪ Don't sleep in the subway </i>♪

1354
00:53:33,010 --> 00:53:33,977
Oh, hi.

1355
00:53:35,179 --> 00:53:36,714
Where did you just come from?

1356
00:53:37,214 --> 00:53:38,348
If I wanted to kill Polk,

1357
00:53:38,415 --> 00:53:40,350
I wouldn't be out here
waiting to talk to you about it.

1358
00:53:40,451 --> 00:53:42,019
Don't try and paint yourself white.

1359
00:53:42,419 --> 00:53:43,721
I'm not.

1360
00:53:43,787 --> 00:53:45,456
I'm the same man
that's wanted in three states

1361
00:53:45,522 --> 00:53:47,091
and five territories, remember?

1362
00:53:47,157 --> 00:53:48,659
[Crow] And I'm not allowed
in the Sizzler.

1363
00:53:48,726 --> 00:53:50,627
Tell me, am I wanted around here?

1364
00:53:50,694 --> 00:53:51,729
[Joel] Don't start.

1365
00:53:52,529 --> 00:53:53,397
Not yet.

1366
00:53:54,465 --> 00:53:56,166
I've only got three more days, huh?

1367
00:53:56,233 --> 00:53:57,668
So have I.

1368
00:53:57,735 --> 00:53:59,336
What do you mean by that?

1369
00:53:59,403 --> 00:54:01,138
Until Sam Bass comes to take over.

1370
00:54:01,939 --> 00:54:03,307
Ah.

1371
00:54:03,373 --> 00:54:05,275
[Joel] Man, look what's coming
out of your horse.

1372
00:54:05,342 --> 00:54:07,111
Look, let's go back to town together.

1373
00:54:11,381 --> 00:54:14,151
Welcome, Rice Lake Key Club.
Music by Tangent.

1374
00:54:14,218 --> 00:54:15,152
See you around.

1375
00:54:15,219 --> 00:54:17,321
Later. I have some special business.

1376
00:54:17,387 --> 00:54:18,655
What kind of business?

1377
00:54:18,722 --> 00:54:20,758
I told you before, it's private.

1378
00:54:20,824 --> 00:54:21,925
But I tell you what,

1379
00:54:21,992 --> 00:54:23,827
meet me just outside of town
where the road forks

1380
00:54:23,894 --> 00:54:25,462
and I'll tell you all about it.

1381
00:54:25,529 --> 00:54:26,530
That a promise?

1382
00:54:26,597 --> 00:54:28,866
Make it tomorrow night at eight o'clock.

1383
00:54:28,932 --> 00:54:29,900
[Crow] Hi. Can I hear this?

1384
00:54:29,967 --> 00:54:30,934
Why not today?

1385
00:54:31,001 --> 00:54:33,337
I'm busy. Tomorrow at eight.

1386
00:54:33,403 --> 00:54:35,773
[Servo] Are you picking me up?
What should I wear?

1387
00:54:35,839 --> 00:54:37,040
Joshua, climb to your horse.

1388
00:54:37,107 --> 00:54:38,041
Hurry up.

1389
00:54:38,108 --> 00:54:40,444
-What's goin' on?
-Quick! We haven't a minute to lose.

1390
00:54:40,511 --> 00:54:42,913
[Joel] OK, give me a minute.
I just woke up.

1391
00:54:43,180 --> 00:54:46,083
[♪♪♪]

1392
00:54:46,150 --> 00:54:49,119
[Crow] So she followed him
and he followed her,

1393
00:54:49,186 --> 00:54:50,988
and now she's following him following her?

1394
00:54:51,054 --> 00:54:52,856
-[Joel] Uh, yeah.
-[Crow shudders]

1395
00:54:54,191 --> 00:54:56,860
[Joel] Looks like the terror
of tiny town got bigger.

1396
00:54:59,096 --> 00:55:00,297
[Servo] Call the office and tell them

1397
00:55:00,364 --> 00:55:02,232
to fax a pair of handcuffs to us.

1398
00:55:08,705 --> 00:55:10,841
[Servo mocking
the film's dramatic music theme]

1399
00:55:12,643 --> 00:55:15,145
[Crow] Careful, traffic
from left does not stop.

1400
00:55:18,048 --> 00:55:19,283
[Joel] What you thinking about?

1401
00:55:21,218 --> 00:55:23,187
[Servo] Easy Snap Ranch,
ready to assemble.

1402
00:55:23,253 --> 00:55:24,721
On your horse, Mayor!

1403
00:55:24,788 --> 00:55:25,656
What is it?

1404
00:55:26,690 --> 00:55:27,724
Cane Miro.

1405
00:55:27,791 --> 00:55:29,126
-[Joel] Oh, Poopy.
-Hurry up.

1406
00:55:31,328 --> 00:55:32,362
-[Crow groans]
-Faster!

1407
00:55:32,429 --> 00:55:34,231
[Crow] Don't watch.
I can't do it when you're watching.

1408
00:55:36,500 --> 00:55:38,001
Come on, come on! Let's go.

1409
00:55:38,068 --> 00:55:39,536
[Joel] I'm doing it!

1410
00:55:39,603 --> 00:55:40,470
Come on, boy.

1411
00:55:41,505 --> 00:55:42,539
[Servo] What was that thing there?

1412
00:55:42,606 --> 00:55:44,107
[Crow] Whatever it is,
it wasn't invented yet.

1413
00:55:44,174 --> 00:55:45,209
[Servo] Mm-hmm.

1414
00:55:45,275 --> 00:55:47,778
[♪♪♪]

1415
00:55:47,845 --> 00:55:50,581
[Joel] Ah, this Greasewood Canyon's
real pretty.

1416
00:55:50,647 --> 00:55:52,316
I was picturing a lot of grease and stuff.

1417
00:55:52,382 --> 00:55:53,417
No grease at all...

1418
00:55:53,483 --> 00:55:55,052
-...just like anywhere else.
-[Servo] Clean.

1419
00:55:57,588 --> 00:55:59,356
[Crow] He was hiding out
at Wall Drug.

1420
00:56:01,191 --> 00:56:02,559
[Joel] Pretty nice. Like the cedar.

1421
00:56:02,626 --> 00:56:05,462
Oh! Done a lot of work here,
added a sunroom back here.

1422
00:56:08,699 --> 00:56:09,800
[Crow] I can't wear black.

1423
00:56:14,271 --> 00:56:17,241
[Joel] Oh, what a mess,
there's garbage everywhere.

1424
00:56:17,307 --> 00:56:19,142
[Servo as horse]
Need any help, boss?

1425
00:56:21,211 --> 00:56:23,213
[Crow] "Dear Steve,
stopped by, you weren't here,

1426
00:56:23,280 --> 00:56:24,781
"borrowed some pants and a blouse,

1427
00:56:24,848 --> 00:56:26,116
"hope you don't mind.

1428
00:56:27,050 --> 00:56:27,918
Keith."

1429
00:56:28,352 --> 00:56:30,454
All right, Herman, back to sleep.

1430
00:56:30,520 --> 00:56:31,955
[Servo] Sheriff took me walking today.

1431
00:56:32,022 --> 00:56:33,724
[Crow] Attica. Attica.

1432
00:56:33,790 --> 00:56:35,292
-[Crow] Oh, forget it.
-What'd he do?

1433
00:56:36,693 --> 00:56:38,595
-How's it going?
-[Joel] Calling it "Leaves of Grass".

1434
00:56:38,662 --> 00:56:42,866
Well, it's not Windsor Castle,
but if it'll keep a killer in,

1435
00:56:42,933 --> 00:56:44,902
it can keep a killer out.

1436
00:56:44,968 --> 00:56:46,169
[Servo] Well, he could shoot you.

1437
00:56:48,605 --> 00:56:49,773
[Crow] Well, I hope
this isn't a conjugal visit.

1438
00:56:49,840 --> 00:56:50,807
-Hello, Felicity.
-Gideon!

1439
00:56:50,874 --> 00:56:52,776
[Joel] Ooh, this is better
than FantaSuites.

1440
00:56:52,843 --> 00:56:54,578
I'm gonna take the cure.

1441
00:56:54,645 --> 00:56:55,846
[Crow] What, Rogaine?

1442
00:56:57,381 --> 00:56:59,349
[♪♪♪]

1443
00:56:59,416 --> 00:57:02,185
{\an8}[Joel] Man, this week
has really dragged on.

1444
00:57:04,955 --> 00:57:07,658
[Servo] Oh, I just couldn't.
With the drunk looking right at us.

1445
00:57:07,724 --> 00:57:09,493
-[Servo] Honey...
-I wish Rose would get back.

1446
00:57:10,160 --> 00:57:11,795
I don't like it when she's away.

1447
00:57:11,862 --> 00:57:14,264
Don't worry, Mayor Polk.
I'll talk care of you.

1448
00:57:14,331 --> 00:57:16,199
Where are your cannons, Captain?

1449
00:57:16,266 --> 00:57:17,434
That's far enough, mister.
You get out of here.

1450
00:57:17,501 --> 00:57:19,102
I'll get out of here when I'm ready.

1451
00:57:19,169 --> 00:57:20,971
Look out, Captain. Yankees comin'.

1452
00:57:21,038 --> 00:57:22,005
I said out.

1453
00:57:24,141 --> 00:57:25,575
[Crow] All right, I was just leaving.

1454
00:57:28,946 --> 00:57:30,080
[Servo] Ow.

1455
00:57:31,448 --> 00:57:33,483
[Servo] I like Wade,
he's just not of dancer.

1456
00:57:37,821 --> 00:57:39,823
[Joel] Man, this movie
is just sitting on my head

1457
00:57:39,890 --> 00:57:41,024
and crushing it.

1458
00:57:42,926 --> 00:57:45,662
[Crow] Ooh, right in
my vast doughy midsection.

1459
00:57:46,129 --> 00:57:48,532
[all whooping like monkeys]

1460
00:57:51,234 --> 00:57:53,670
[Servo] Not exactly the riot at Alcatraz.

1461
00:57:53,737 --> 00:57:56,273
[men grunting]

1462
00:57:56,340 --> 00:57:58,575
[Joel] Whoa, watch
the bumper pool table! Oh...

1463
00:57:58,642 --> 00:57:59,710
[Crow] Well...

1464
00:58:04,448 --> 00:58:05,415
[Servo] Well...?

1465
00:58:06,183 --> 00:58:08,352
[Crow] Whoa, there goes
the facade. Almost.

1466
00:58:08,418 --> 00:58:09,820
[Joel] Close.

1467
00:58:16,960 --> 00:58:18,528
[Joel] And now it's a hat
made out of an udder.

1468
00:58:21,164 --> 00:58:23,300
-[Servo] Wilton Palmeter.
-What happened here?

1469
00:58:23,367 --> 00:58:24,568
He tried to kill me.

1470
00:58:25,302 --> 00:58:26,770
I wouldn't spit on him.

1471
00:58:26,837 --> 00:58:28,171
Joshua saved my life.

1472
00:58:28,238 --> 00:58:29,840
[Servo] We will return
to Non-Sequitur Theater.

1473
00:58:29,906 --> 00:58:31,742
Alright, clear out.
We'll worry about this later.

1474
00:58:33,210 --> 00:58:34,144
I'll see you later.

1475
00:58:34,211 --> 00:58:35,078
I'll think about it.

1476
00:58:35,746 --> 00:58:37,647
[Crow] We're still on
for 8:00 though, aren't we?

1477
00:58:39,916 --> 00:58:41,418
[Joel] Good one, Brad.

1478
00:58:42,119 --> 00:58:43,353
I'm all right, Miss Rose.

1479
00:58:43,420 --> 00:58:45,922
Next time, Joshua,
if you have to, use a gun.

1480
00:58:45,989 --> 00:58:47,357
I didn't give him a chance
to try anything.

1481
00:58:47,424 --> 00:58:48,859
[Servo] I'm not that kind of girl.

1482
00:58:49,426 --> 00:58:50,861
I'm going over to Red Dog.

1483
00:58:50,927 --> 00:58:52,529
[Joel] They're hiring dancers.

1484
00:58:52,596 --> 00:58:53,897
[Servo] You big galoot.

1485
00:58:55,866 --> 00:58:57,234
Sally upstairs?

1486
00:58:57,300 --> 00:58:59,269
-She's tripping.
-That's a switch.

1487
00:58:59,870 --> 00:59:01,004
Well, I'm going to pay
you girls off today

1488
00:59:01,071 --> 00:59:02,906
so you can get an early start tomorrow.

1489
00:59:03,774 --> 00:59:05,142
I sure hate to go.

1490
00:59:05,909 --> 00:59:06,877
I hate to lose you.

1491
00:59:06,943 --> 00:59:08,645
[Crow] It's been so fun
with you and everybody.

1492
00:59:08,712 --> 00:59:10,347
...rough time finding three more girls.

1493
00:59:10,847 --> 00:59:11,982
Poor Erica.

1494
00:59:12,449 --> 00:59:13,450
Why don't you get out of those pants

1495
00:59:13,517 --> 00:59:15,252
-and find yourself a man?
-[Servo] Woof.

1496
00:59:15,318 --> 00:59:16,920
I'm wearing these pants
because I lost a man,

1497
00:59:16,987 --> 00:59:18,488
a better man than ever
slipped you a dollar.

1498
00:59:18,555 --> 00:59:19,489
[Joel] Ouch.

1499
00:59:19,556 --> 00:59:20,824
There's no law against tipping.

1500
00:59:21,525 --> 00:59:22,592
Sundown tomorrow?

1501
00:59:23,293 --> 00:59:24,461
They're leaving in the morning.

1502
00:59:25,128 --> 00:59:27,230
I just wanted to make sure
everything was clear.

1503
00:59:27,297 --> 00:59:28,899
-[Servo] Well...
-Bye, girls.

1504
00:59:28,965 --> 00:59:30,567
[Servo, Joel and Crow]
Bye.

1505
00:59:30,634 --> 00:59:32,335
What's she got against us anyway?

1506
00:59:33,336 --> 00:59:35,472
She thinks you violated
the sanitary code.

1507
00:59:35,539 --> 00:59:36,740
[Servo] That's my job.

1508
00:59:36,807 --> 00:59:38,341
I could kill that woman.

1509
00:59:39,643 --> 00:59:41,344
Why, Tessie, that's against the law.

1510
00:59:41,411 --> 00:59:42,879
[Crow] I still want to.

1511
00:59:43,680 --> 00:59:46,683
'Course, it could be
a coincidental accident.

1512
00:59:47,951 --> 00:59:48,885
With dear Rose gone,

1513
00:59:48,952 --> 00:59:50,120
you'd have no reason to leave town.

1514
00:59:50,187 --> 00:59:52,889
[Joel] She's paying them
in television warranties.

1515
00:59:52,956 --> 00:59:54,157
Girls, you've been so good for business

1516
00:59:54,224 --> 00:59:56,193
I'm going to give you
a little going-away bonus.

1517
00:59:56,259 --> 00:59:57,260
Wampum bucks.

1518
01:00:00,197 --> 01:00:01,298
[Servo] Hey...

1519
01:00:05,735 --> 01:00:08,505
[Joel] Well, I'll see if I can
borrow a dollar from Ed.

1520
01:00:14,277 --> 01:00:16,446
-Hello, there.
-[Servo] I thought you were Dale.

1521
01:00:17,280 --> 01:00:19,149
What are you doing up there?

1522
01:00:19,683 --> 01:00:21,418
On the lookout for gorgeous marshals.

1523
01:00:21,485 --> 01:00:22,486
[Crow mocks laughter]

1524
01:00:22,552 --> 01:00:23,753
You didn't need to
scare me half to death.

1525
01:00:23,820 --> 01:00:24,988
Come on up.

1526
01:00:25,889 --> 01:00:27,390
Don't be silly.

1527
01:00:27,491 --> 01:00:29,025
You wanna learn my business, don't ya?

1528
01:00:29,092 --> 01:00:30,160
[Crow] You did your business up there?

1529
01:00:30,227 --> 01:00:31,895
I almost didn't come at all.

1530
01:00:31,962 --> 01:00:34,131
I almost didn't expect you.

1531
01:00:34,197 --> 01:00:35,999
But now that you're here,
if you want to find out anything,

1532
01:00:36,066 --> 01:00:37,501
you'll have to come up in this tree.

1533
01:00:37,567 --> 01:00:39,302
[Joel] I made
a really cool fort up here.

1534
01:00:39,369 --> 01:00:43,039
-Twelve-year-old!
-I spent that much time in prison.

1535
01:00:43,106 --> 01:00:45,275
-All right, little boy, I'll come up.
-[Servo groans]

1536
01:00:45,342 --> 01:00:47,377
[Servo] Gee, you're not
as small as you look.

1537
01:00:47,444 --> 01:00:48,411
[panting]

1538
01:00:48,478 --> 01:00:50,747
[Crow] You can make me feel
young again.

1539
01:00:50,814 --> 01:00:52,849
All right, start talking.

1540
01:00:52,916 --> 01:00:54,985
[Servo babbling]

1541
01:00:55,852 --> 01:00:58,321
Look, you can see the Big Dipper.

1542
01:00:58,388 --> 01:00:59,456
[Joel] Hey, it's daytime.

1543
01:00:59,523 --> 01:01:00,490
[Crow] He's not talking about the stars.

1544
01:01:00,557 --> 01:01:01,725
[Joel] I don't know.

1545
01:01:01,791 --> 01:01:04,761
-Well, come down from the stars.
-[Servo] OK.

1546
01:01:04,828 --> 01:01:06,930
I want to know exactly
what you're after here.

1547
01:01:08,532 --> 01:01:09,633
Very little.

1548
01:01:09,699 --> 01:01:11,635
[Servo] Just this.

1549
01:01:11,835 --> 01:01:13,336
[Servo vocalizing eating]

1550
01:01:19,209 --> 01:01:20,343
I know all about that.

1551
01:01:20,410 --> 01:01:22,245
[Joel] We had a class in fifth grade.

1552
01:01:22,879 --> 01:01:24,114
I mean, other things.

1553
01:01:24,981 --> 01:01:26,149
What other things?

1554
01:01:27,484 --> 01:01:29,319
-Oh...
-[Crow] Tasty Freeze.

1555
01:01:29,386 --> 01:01:30,620
...things about Oracle.

1556
01:01:32,756 --> 01:01:33,823
Nice place.

1557
01:01:33,890 --> 01:01:35,792
[Joel] Hear they got
a meat packing plant there.

1558
01:01:37,827 --> 01:01:39,362
You tried to kill Polk today.

1559
01:01:40,163 --> 01:01:42,299
-I love you.
-I'm glad you didn't get to him.

1560
01:01:42,365 --> 01:01:43,567
I'd have had to kill you.

1561
01:01:43,633 --> 01:01:46,069
[Crow] Now he's the sensitive
coldblooded killer.

1562
01:01:47,504 --> 01:01:49,072
But you didn't.

1563
01:01:49,139 --> 01:01:50,340
I love you.

1564
01:01:50,407 --> 01:01:51,808
[Servo] Hmph.

1565
01:01:51,875 --> 01:01:53,343
I thought that's what you said.

1566
01:01:55,512 --> 01:01:56,846
I'm glad you're here.

1567
01:01:56,913 --> 01:02:00,016
[Servo] So how's this going to effect
his contract to kill her, I wonder?

1568
01:02:03,019 --> 01:02:05,589
[Joel] Tastiest sheriff
in the Old West.

1569
01:02:05,655 --> 01:02:06,823
I wish that...

1570
01:02:07,390 --> 01:02:09,059
-What?
-[Crow] You were somebody else.

1571
01:02:09,125 --> 01:02:12,062
[sighs] I have to throw you out and I...

1572
01:02:12,128 --> 01:02:13,396
[Joel] Motel matches.

1573
01:02:13,463 --> 01:02:14,898
...I wish I didn't have to.

1574
01:02:15,599 --> 01:02:17,267
No one's making you do anything.

1575
01:02:18,602 --> 01:02:19,769
I won't change my mind...

1576
01:02:19,836 --> 01:02:21,938
[Servo] Well, maybe I will.
No, no I won't.

1577
01:02:22,005 --> 01:02:23,406
...but I can make-believe a little.

1578
01:02:24,708 --> 01:02:27,544
Sure you can. We both can.

1579
01:02:27,611 --> 01:02:29,613
[Crow] Let's make-believe
I have talent.

1580
01:02:29,679 --> 01:02:32,082
Did you tell anyone I ordered you
out of town by Saturday?

1581
01:02:33,016 --> 01:02:34,084
Not a soul.

1582
01:02:34,985 --> 01:02:36,753
Well, pretend I'm taking it all back.

1583
01:02:37,454 --> 01:02:39,289
You stay here forever and I'll...

1584
01:02:39,356 --> 01:02:40,724
[Servo] Aw, forget it.

1585
01:02:43,193 --> 01:02:44,227
You didn't tell anyone?

1586
01:02:45,161 --> 01:02:46,196
That's what I said.

1587
01:02:48,064 --> 01:02:49,499
Except Erica.

1588
01:02:49,566 --> 01:02:50,800
Erica, last of all.

1589
01:02:50,867 --> 01:02:52,836
[Servo] No, she was
the last person I didn't tell.

1590
01:02:53,837 --> 01:02:55,038
You're lying to me.

1591
01:02:55,105 --> 01:02:56,206
I wouldn't lie to you.

1592
01:02:56,273 --> 01:02:58,008
She knows. She told Polk.

1593
01:02:58,074 --> 01:03:00,744
-[Crow] OK, I would lie to you.
-So she knows.

1594
01:03:01,745 --> 01:03:04,281
-We're making believe, aren't we?
-That isn't why you lied.

1595
01:03:05,382 --> 01:03:06,883
How does Erica fit into your plans?

1596
01:03:06,950 --> 01:03:09,085
[Joel] What is this?
Come on, let's love!

1597
01:03:09,152 --> 01:03:10,287
Is she in this tree?

1598
01:03:13,390 --> 01:03:14,324
I don't know.

1599
01:03:15,525 --> 01:03:16,593
Is she?

1600
01:03:17,961 --> 01:03:19,129
Don't be a fool.

1601
01:03:19,195 --> 01:03:20,563
[Servo speaks French]

1602
01:03:20,630 --> 01:03:21,765
[Servo] What's that, baby?

1603
01:03:21,831 --> 01:03:23,933
It means, may I borrow your bicycle?

1604
01:03:24,868 --> 01:03:26,236
I can't trust you.

1605
01:03:27,137 --> 01:03:28,204
I know you can't.

1606
01:03:29,306 --> 01:03:30,473
I'd laugh at anyone that did...

1607
01:03:30,540 --> 01:03:32,042
[Joel] Ha ha.

1608
01:03:32,108 --> 01:03:33,943
...but I swear to you
I was telling God's truth

1609
01:03:34,010 --> 01:03:35,178
when I said I loved you.

1610
01:03:35,712 --> 01:03:36,946
Maybe you were, Cane.

1611
01:03:38,748 --> 01:03:42,018
Maybe it's a two-way thing.

1612
01:03:42,085 --> 01:03:43,953
[Crow] With a center passing lane.

1613
01:03:44,020 --> 01:03:46,189
-But there's one thing I mustn't forget...
-[Joel] Jello.

1614
01:03:46,256 --> 01:03:48,291
...and that's that we're
sworn enemies, you and I.

1615
01:03:48,358 --> 01:03:50,760
All the moonlight in heaven
can't change that.

1616
01:03:50,827 --> 01:03:52,228
[Servo] Oh yeah, that's right.

1617
01:03:54,097 --> 01:03:55,732
[Crow] It's too late
to create conflict.

1618
01:03:55,799 --> 01:03:57,100
-[Servo] Mm-hmm.
-Goodnight, Cane.

1619
01:03:58,168 --> 01:04:00,337
[Joel] She is one spooky chick.

1620
01:04:06,609 --> 01:04:07,911
[Joel] My enemies don't realize

1621
01:04:07,977 --> 01:04:10,347
that I'm very vulnerable right now.

1622
01:04:13,650 --> 01:04:16,319
[Joel] What is the crew
doing in this shot?

1623
01:04:16,386 --> 01:04:17,854
[Crow] In this movie,
you can just pick any object

1624
01:04:17,921 --> 01:04:19,089
and hide behind it.

1625
01:04:19,155 --> 01:04:20,156
Let go of me!

1626
01:04:20,223 --> 01:04:21,925
[Servo] All right, what are these?

1627
01:04:21,991 --> 01:04:24,494
[Joel] Looks like they've
all been to Fleet Farm.

1628
01:04:26,463 --> 01:04:27,497
[Rose] What are you doing?

1629
01:04:27,564 --> 01:04:29,032
[Servo] This is for taking my lip liner.

1630
01:04:29,099 --> 01:04:31,134
[Crow] She's been attacked
by Babes in Toyland.

1631
01:04:31,634 --> 01:04:33,503
-[Servo] And the grunge look here.
-[Crow] Oh, yes.

1632
01:04:33,570 --> 01:04:36,306
[Joel] You're going to watch us dance
if it's the last thing you do.

1633
01:04:39,609 --> 01:04:41,511
[Servo] Oh, come on,
you know I don't wear necklaces.

1634
01:04:41,578 --> 01:04:42,779
Stop it! Let go!

1635
01:04:42,846 --> 01:04:44,414
-Stop!
-[Joel] This isn't funny!

1636
01:04:44,481 --> 01:04:45,648
[♪♪♪]

1637
01:04:46,282 --> 01:04:47,450
Don't let 'em get away!

1638
01:04:48,284 --> 01:04:49,486
[gunshot]

1639
01:04:50,153 --> 01:04:51,821
Don't bother going back to town.

1640
01:04:51,888 --> 01:04:53,857
I want you out of this state tonight.

1641
01:04:53,957 --> 01:04:56,459
-What about our clothes?
-Now!

1642
01:04:57,060 --> 01:04:58,128
If you ever come back to Oracle again,

1643
01:04:58,194 --> 01:04:59,195
I'll kill all three of you.

1644
01:04:59,262 --> 01:05:00,897
[Crow] I'm just so upset right now.

1645
01:05:00,964 --> 01:05:01,998
Move!

1646
01:05:03,199 --> 01:05:04,567
[Joel] This bites. Let's go, Gretel.

1647
01:05:04,634 --> 01:05:07,404
-[Crow] Told you it wouldn't work.
-[Servo] It wasn't my idea, Cindy.

1648
01:05:07,470 --> 01:05:09,105
My new shirt.

1649
01:05:09,172 --> 01:05:10,440
[hoofbeats departing]

1650
01:05:10,507 --> 01:05:12,442
[Crow] She didn't even cry
when her husband died.

1651
01:05:12,509 --> 01:05:13,710
[Servo] Ah! Ow! Ow!

1652
01:05:14,978 --> 01:05:17,714
{\an8}[Joel] The British were coming!
The British were coming!

1653
01:05:18,648 --> 01:05:19,916
[Servo] Little man, my man.

1654
01:05:22,719 --> 01:05:23,820
[Crow] And action.

1655
01:05:25,755 --> 01:05:27,257
What's the matter? You goin' home?

1656
01:05:28,892 --> 01:05:31,194
That was a smart stunt
you tried to pull last night.

1657
01:05:31,761 --> 01:05:32,862
What are you talking about?

1658
01:05:33,730 --> 01:05:35,832
You think you can get away
with sicking your floozies on Rose?

1659
01:05:35,899 --> 01:05:36,933
[Servo] I thought I might.

1660
01:05:37,000 --> 01:05:38,435
How did you know about that?

1661
01:05:38,535 --> 01:05:40,770
I saw the whole thing.
They tried to hang her.

1662
01:05:40,837 --> 01:05:41,771
Where?

1663
01:05:41,838 --> 01:05:43,940
Three miles out, just off the main road.

1664
01:05:44,474 --> 01:05:45,842
What were you doing there?

1665
01:05:45,942 --> 01:05:47,844
That's none of your business.

1666
01:05:47,944 --> 01:05:49,946
That woman's my target tomorrow,

1667
01:05:50,013 --> 01:05:51,514
and you're my hired help.

1668
01:05:52,148 --> 01:05:55,285
Everything you and she do
in this town is my business.

1669
01:05:55,385 --> 01:05:57,053
Don't flatter yourself.

1670
01:05:58,021 --> 01:05:59,589
I'll see you in your room tonight.

1671
01:06:00,523 --> 01:06:02,559
[Crow] It's a hallway,
and don't you forget it!

1672
01:06:04,394 --> 01:06:05,628
[Servo] What it is, little Wormy guy.

1673
01:06:06,963 --> 01:06:08,932
[Servo with nasally voice]
I never liked him.

1674
01:06:08,998 --> 01:06:10,366
[♪♪♪]

1675
01:06:10,433 --> 01:06:13,203
-[Crow] Mmm, pure maple syrup.
-Well, tomorrow's the big day.

1676
01:06:13,269 --> 01:06:16,239
-[Servo] Yeah. Who the hell are you?
-Yeah, big day.

1677
01:06:19,709 --> 01:06:22,111
[Joel] Right in the crotch,
I did it again. Ooh.

1678
01:06:24,047 --> 01:06:27,116
[Servo] The man
who shot Vivian Valance.

1679
01:06:27,951 --> 01:06:29,586
[Joel] His hands are glowing.

1680
01:06:29,986 --> 01:06:32,822
[♪♪♪]

1681
01:06:32,889 --> 01:06:34,924
[Crow] Booze, it's what's for dinner.

1682
01:06:34,991 --> 01:06:37,794
[Servo] The perdiest marshal
of the Old West.

1683
01:06:39,996 --> 01:06:41,898
Why don't you do your
drinking in your room, Cane?

1684
01:06:41,965 --> 01:06:44,267
-[Servo] It's a hall.
-Am I disturbing the peace?

1685
01:06:44,901 --> 01:06:48,004
I do disturb the peace
sometimes, you know.

1686
01:06:48,104 --> 01:06:49,939
-I was thinking of you.
-[Servo humming somber theme]

1687
01:06:50,573 --> 01:06:52,375
Well, don't be sorry, beautiful.

1688
01:06:53,409 --> 01:06:56,145
Tonight's the last night for you and me.

1689
01:06:56,246 --> 01:06:58,815
In the morning, we'll both be done.

1690
01:06:58,915 --> 01:07:00,216
Go away.

1691
01:07:01,351 --> 01:07:03,786
There are better ways to say goodbye.

1692
01:07:03,853 --> 01:07:04,888
Are there?

1693
01:07:04,954 --> 01:07:05,955
[Crow] Are you saying
what I think you're saying?

1694
01:07:06,022 --> 01:07:07,724
<i>Find the one that feels good.</i>

1695
01:07:09,659 --> 01:07:10,660
No?

1696
01:07:10,727 --> 01:07:12,629
[Joel] Ouch, there I go again.

1697
01:07:12,695 --> 01:07:13,630
<i>Get out of here and leave me alone.</i>

1698
01:07:13,696 --> 01:07:15,098
<i>I don't want to see you or touch you</i>

1699
01:07:15,164 --> 01:07:17,567
<i>or ever remember that I knew you.</i>

1700
01:07:17,700 --> 01:07:19,536
[Servo continues humming
somber theme]

1701
01:07:19,602 --> 01:07:20,637
<i>You don't mean that.</i>

1702
01:07:23,172 --> 01:07:27,176
<i>More than anything I ever</i>
<i>meant in my life, I mean that.</i>

1703
01:07:27,243 --> 01:07:28,912
[Crow] Except there was something
I said a while back

1704
01:07:28,978 --> 01:07:30,413
that I meant more than that.

1705
01:07:30,480 --> 01:07:33,550
[Servo continues humming
somber theme]

1706
01:07:33,616 --> 01:07:36,419
[Joel] Hey, the Angel of Death's
stopping by for a drink.

1707
01:07:36,486 --> 01:07:37,587
[Crow] Well, that's nice.

1708
01:07:38,855 --> 01:07:40,857
[Joel] Darn zipper, stuck again.

1709
01:07:46,162 --> 01:07:47,830
[Servo] Everything I need to know
I learn from booze.

1710
01:07:47,897 --> 01:07:49,832
-[knocking on door]
-[Servo] Come out.

1711
01:07:51,634 --> 01:07:52,502
[Joel gulps]

1712
01:07:53,269 --> 01:07:55,638
[Crow] Uh. Right in the middle of dinner.

1713
01:07:58,441 --> 01:07:59,609
[Joel imitating drunk]
Uh... OK.

1714
01:07:59,676 --> 01:08:02,178
Who wants to come
into the hallway now?

1715
01:08:02,845 --> 01:08:05,114
-You drunk.
<i>-[slurs] Come on in, Erica.</i>

1716
01:08:05,848 --> 01:08:07,817
<i>You and I are on the same side.</i>

1717
01:08:07,884 --> 01:08:09,018
<i>What are you talking about?</i>

1718
01:08:09,085 --> 01:08:10,753
[Servo] We're humans, come here.

1719
01:08:13,890 --> 01:08:15,291
<i>Who cares what I'm talking about?</i>

1720
01:08:15,358 --> 01:08:16,893
<i>I should keep you drunk all the time.</i>

1721
01:08:16,960 --> 01:08:19,696
[Crow] I am.
We are. Or something.

1722
01:08:21,097 --> 01:08:25,001
[Servo] Sneak, sneak,
sneak, sneak, squeak.

1723
01:08:25,068 --> 01:08:26,836
[Joel] Oh... Mmm.

1724
01:08:27,837 --> 01:08:29,372
<i>You got brown eyes.</i>

1725
01:08:29,439 --> 01:08:31,307
[Servo] Uh, you got a neck.

1726
01:08:32,976 --> 01:08:34,077
<i>I come here to battle with you,</i>

1727
01:08:34,143 --> 01:08:36,613
and you start talking
<i>about the color of my eyes.</i>

1728
01:08:36,679 --> 01:08:39,282
[Servo] You got, uh,
large pores on your nose.

1729
01:08:39,349 --> 01:08:40,883
Oh, and a wood tick. Mmm.

1730
01:08:41,985 --> 01:08:43,519
<i>You're a darn fool.</i>

1731
01:08:43,586 --> 01:08:45,088
<i>That's what I am.</i>

1732
01:08:45,154 --> 01:08:46,756
<i>I'm a lovin' fool.</i>

1733
01:08:47,490 --> 01:08:48,658
<i>Lovin' fool.</i>

1734
01:08:49,025 --> 01:08:51,594
[Joel] You taste
like Annie Greensprings.

1735
01:08:51,661 --> 01:08:52,762
<i>And you'll never stop?</i>

1736
01:08:53,830 --> 01:08:55,365
<i>Who wants to sober up?</i>

1737
01:08:56,099 --> 01:08:58,701
[Servo imitating drunk] Booze has
knighted me the king of the lovers.

1738
01:08:59,402 --> 01:09:00,670
<i>You're mean when you're sober.</i>

1739
01:09:00,737 --> 01:09:02,205
<i>I'm not mean.</i>

1740
01:09:02,305 --> 01:09:04,774
I love everybody,
<i>and especially I love Erica.</i>

1741
01:09:04,841 --> 01:09:06,142
[Servo] Hey, guys,
look at little theory to put forth

1742
01:09:06,209 --> 01:09:09,178
about how he got around in
the back of the building there

1743
01:09:09,245 --> 01:09:11,014
and came around on the horse and...

1744
01:09:19,188 --> 01:09:20,757
But Tom, that doesn't explain

1745
01:09:20,823 --> 01:09:23,192
how John Ireland could go
into the attorney's office

1746
01:09:23,259 --> 01:09:25,928
and suddenly appear
on his horse in the street?

1747
01:09:25,995 --> 01:09:28,898
Look, Joel, it's really just
a broadened interpretation

1748
01:09:28,965 --> 01:09:30,833
of quantum linear super positional.

1749
01:09:30,900 --> 01:09:32,268
Super behud-- Huh?

1750
01:09:32,368 --> 01:09:33,870
They simply observe
the apparent relative state

1751
01:09:33,936 --> 01:09:36,773
of John Ireland in one place,
while in actuality

1752
01:09:36,839 --> 01:09:39,008
he coexisted
in the objective vector state.

1753
01:09:39,075 --> 01:09:41,010
-You see?
-I have a theory.

1754
01:09:41,077 --> 01:09:42,578
That town is a bunch of false fronts

1755
01:09:42,645 --> 01:09:43,813
and he ran over there real fast.

1756
01:09:43,880 --> 01:09:44,947
All right, I'm with him.

1757
01:09:45,014 --> 01:09:46,983
Guys, why is it so hard
to accept the fact

1758
01:09:47,050 --> 01:09:49,419
that time is not an immutable
forward progression,

1759
01:09:49,485 --> 01:09:51,120
but a factor in a space time model

1760
01:09:51,187 --> 01:09:54,157
of relativistic causality
and determinism, huh?

1761
01:09:54,223 --> 01:09:56,325
Guys? Hello?

1762
01:09:56,392 --> 01:09:57,660
Geez, like a couple of cattle, these two.

1763
01:09:57,727 --> 01:09:58,594
OK. [clears throat]

1764
01:09:58,661 --> 01:10:00,096
Here, I'm going to demonstrate, OK?

1765
01:10:00,163 --> 01:10:01,731
Watch me closely.

1766
01:10:02,298 --> 01:10:04,200
Alleoop!

1767
01:10:04,267 --> 01:10:05,334
Hey, wait, where did he go?

1768
01:10:05,401 --> 01:10:07,170
-I don't know. He just--
-I'm over here, guys.

1769
01:10:07,236 --> 01:10:09,372
-Aaghh!
-I hate when you do that.

1770
01:10:09,439 --> 01:10:12,008
But, Servo, that's fantastic,
that's amazing.

1771
01:10:12,075 --> 01:10:13,976
It's physics, Joel, plain and simple.

1772
01:10:14,043 --> 01:10:16,846
You just exist in one
observable region in space,

1773
01:10:16,913 --> 01:10:20,583
and then zip, you simply realign
your point of origin, you see?

1774
01:10:20,650 --> 01:10:21,784
He does this to me at night.

1775
01:10:21,851 --> 01:10:22,885
Scared the hell out of me.

1776
01:10:22,952 --> 01:10:24,787
It's easy, guys.
A trained chimp could do it.

1777
01:10:24,854 --> 01:10:26,055
Come on, Joel, try it. It's fun.

1778
01:10:26,122 --> 01:10:29,325
OK, I'm going to excite myself

1779
01:10:29,392 --> 01:10:32,328
-in a position of undetermined...
-Oh, boy.

1780
01:10:32,395 --> 01:10:34,030
origin and region.

1781
01:10:34,097 --> 01:10:36,799
-And zock!
-[Servo] No, no, no.

1782
01:10:36,866 --> 01:10:38,468
-It didn't really work.
-Well, I'm not doing it.

1783
01:10:38,534 --> 01:10:41,237
Doing it makes you chubby
and stupid like Tom.

1784
01:10:41,304 --> 01:10:43,873
-Say it to my face.
-Joel, help me.

1785
01:10:43,940 --> 01:10:46,109
Hey, you know, I can work
space and time this way? What?

1786
01:10:46,175 --> 01:10:47,844
-Oh, Tom, I don't think that...
-[Servo grunts]

1787
01:10:47,910 --> 01:10:50,847
But that still doesn't explain
how John Ireland is able to go

1788
01:10:50,913 --> 01:10:54,684
into the attorney's office
and end up on his horse on this...

1789
01:10:54,751 --> 01:10:56,819
-[scoffs] What the...?
-[Servo laughs]

1790
01:10:56,886 --> 01:10:58,020
See what I mean?

1791
01:10:58,488 --> 01:10:59,922
Hey, my sandwich is whole again.

1792
01:10:59,989 --> 01:11:01,090
-[Crow] Cool.
-[Servo] Yeah.

1793
01:11:01,157 --> 01:11:02,358
We-- We'll be right back.

1794
01:11:02,425 --> 01:11:03,359
No, no, no, no.

1795
01:11:03,426 --> 01:11:05,495
They'll be right back,
we'll be right here.

1796
01:11:05,561 --> 01:11:06,696
Honey, don't.

1797
01:11:09,699 --> 01:11:10,967
-You mean that, Cane?
-[Crow] Whoa.

1798
01:11:11,033 --> 01:11:13,236
'Course I mean it. I said it, didn't I?

1799
01:11:14,070 --> 01:11:16,939
And to think I was worried
about poor little Rose.

1800
01:11:19,175 --> 01:11:20,743
[Servo] Magnuson,
puts her into the boards.

1801
01:11:20,810 --> 01:11:21,677
Sorry.

1802
01:11:21,778 --> 01:11:22,845
I have to tell you this...

1803
01:11:22,912 --> 01:11:23,846
[Servo] I'm Pops Staples.

1804
01:11:23,913 --> 01:11:25,014
...there's been a change in plans.

1805
01:11:25,081 --> 01:11:26,783
[Crow] I'm going blonde.

1806
01:11:26,849 --> 01:11:27,950
With the mayor locked up in jail,

1807
01:11:28,017 --> 01:11:29,485
we'll have to get the letter
from the Express rider

1808
01:11:29,552 --> 01:11:31,087
before he gets to town.

1809
01:11:32,121 --> 01:11:33,189
Do you understand?

1810
01:11:33,256 --> 01:11:34,223
[Servo imitating drunk]
You got brown eyes.

1811
01:11:34,290 --> 01:11:35,558
I understand.

1812
01:11:35,658 --> 01:11:38,494
Then I'll meet you
at Immigrant Gap at 6:30.

1813
01:11:40,163 --> 01:11:42,532
[Joel imitating drunk] There are
six immigrants at the Gap. Got it.

1814
01:11:42,598 --> 01:11:44,534
...Immigrant Gap at 6:30.

1815
01:11:44,600 --> 01:11:46,602
[Crow] Booze. Write that down.

1816
01:11:50,206 --> 01:11:52,608
[Joel] Look, a sale at Hurrah.

1817
01:12:00,383 --> 01:12:01,617
[Crow] It's Buddy Love.

1818
01:12:03,986 --> 01:12:06,155
[Joel] Well, better do
next week's schedule.

1819
01:12:08,357 --> 01:12:09,425
[all three] Boo!

1820
01:12:09,492 --> 01:12:11,861
There! You got what you asked for!

1821
01:12:12,628 --> 01:12:14,964
Don't go lying like that again
about how you love me.

1822
01:12:15,031 --> 01:12:15,965
[gasping]

1823
01:12:16,032 --> 01:12:17,767
[Servo stammers] I lurve you.

1824
01:12:18,501 --> 01:12:19,635
I'm gonna kill you.

1825
01:12:20,169 --> 01:12:23,005
I'm gonna kill you
but I'm gonna use Cane Miro to do it.

1826
01:12:23,072 --> 01:12:24,207
All I have to do is pay him,

1827
01:12:24,273 --> 01:12:26,275
and he'll follow you
to the end of the world.

1828
01:12:27,510 --> 01:12:28,678
You won't do that.

1829
01:12:28,744 --> 01:12:30,479
[Crow] Missus, lady, don't, no.

1830
01:12:30,546 --> 01:12:32,515
Jake, you're a dead little man.

1831
01:12:33,049 --> 01:12:35,184
Now get out before I kill you myself.

1832
01:12:36,018 --> 01:12:38,054
[Servo] OK, what time
do you want me in tomorrow?

1833
01:12:40,456 --> 01:12:42,692
[Crow] This is like
<i>Silverado, </i>only better.

1834
01:12:42,758 --> 01:12:43,726
[Joel] Yeah, a lot better.

1835
01:12:45,595 --> 01:12:49,832
[Servo] Joel, I hate my paws so bad.

1836
01:13:00,643 --> 01:13:02,078
[Crow] Huh? Oh, sale at Hurrah.

1837
01:13:06,349 --> 01:13:07,283
Don't shoot me!

1838
01:13:07,350 --> 01:13:08,885
[Servo] Oh, no, I'm the comic relief.
Don't shoot.

1839
01:13:08,951 --> 01:13:11,020
What do you mean by
bursting in here like that?

1840
01:13:11,087 --> 01:13:13,055
You'd better go after Cane Miro.

1841
01:13:13,389 --> 01:13:14,857
Cane? What for?

1842
01:13:14,924 --> 01:13:16,525
He's gonna shoot you.

1843
01:13:16,592 --> 01:13:18,160
[Crow] Over my dead body.

1844
01:13:18,227 --> 01:13:19,362
How do you know that?

1845
01:13:19,428 --> 01:13:21,364
Erica Page hired him to do it.

1846
01:13:21,430 --> 01:13:23,566
I seen her pay him $3,000 to kill you

1847
01:13:23,633 --> 01:13:25,601
if the railroad don't come through Oracle.

1848
01:13:25,668 --> 01:13:26,869
The railroad?

1849
01:13:26,936 --> 01:13:28,905
They're just waiting for you
to read that letter, Mayor.

1850
01:13:28,971 --> 01:13:31,274
-I'd better go after him.
-No. No. You can't.

1851
01:13:31,340 --> 01:13:33,009
You can't arrest a man
on Jake's hearsay.

1852
01:13:33,075 --> 01:13:34,243
You'd better do it!

1853
01:13:34,310 --> 01:13:35,344
I emphatically agree.

1854
01:13:35,411 --> 01:13:37,046
We just have to wait
until he does something.

1855
01:13:37,113 --> 01:13:38,714
By then, it may be too late.

1856
01:13:38,781 --> 01:13:40,416
So Erica paid him.

1857
01:13:41,484 --> 01:13:43,419
She's probably behind
Scott's killing too.

1858
01:13:43,486 --> 01:13:45,888
Sure she is,
and she's in love with Cane Miro

1859
01:13:45,955 --> 01:13:46,889
and him with her too.

1860
01:13:46,956 --> 01:13:49,025
[Joel] Can I hit you,
Wormy, just once?

1861
01:13:49,091 --> 01:13:50,660
Go on, Jake.

1862
01:13:50,726 --> 01:13:52,128
You mean, you're gonna let him be?

1863
01:13:52,194 --> 01:13:53,195
[Servo] Speaking words of wisdom?

1864
01:13:53,262 --> 01:13:55,231
Yeah, that's right.
Goodnight, little man.

1865
01:13:55,298 --> 01:13:58,301
Don't call me that! Erica called me that.

1866
01:13:58,367 --> 01:13:59,435
I don't like it!

1867
01:13:59,502 --> 01:14:01,437
-[Crow] Touched a nerve.
-I don't like it!

1868
01:14:01,504 --> 01:14:03,039
[Joel] We are kind of little.

1869
01:14:04,573 --> 01:14:05,875
You're making a big mistake, Rose.

1870
01:14:06,008 --> 01:14:07,109
[Servo] Stay in school.

1871
01:14:07,176 --> 01:14:08,678
You ought to move in tonight.

1872
01:14:08,778 --> 01:14:11,948
On what evidence?
Jake's testimony?

1873
01:14:12,515 --> 01:14:14,517
Any cheap lawyer would prove
him mentally incompetent

1874
01:14:14,583 --> 01:14:15,518
in three minutes.

1875
01:14:15,584 --> 01:14:17,620
[Joel] Hey, they haven't
invented that yet.

1876
01:14:19,088 --> 01:14:23,092
No, we--we just have to wait it out.

1877
01:14:23,559 --> 01:14:26,128
[Crow] ♪<i> Why am I such a misfit? </i>♪

1878
01:14:27,163 --> 01:14:28,130
Evening, Jake.

1879
01:14:29,665 --> 01:14:30,666
[Servo] I'm a pixie!

1880
01:14:34,370 --> 01:14:36,505
Don't say hi. Come on.

1881
01:14:37,606 --> 01:14:39,141
[Servo] Oh, for crying out loud,
he's upset.

1882
01:14:39,208 --> 01:14:42,111
Little, what's got into you?
Little, honey?

1883
01:14:44,280 --> 01:14:46,482
[♪♪♪]

1884
01:14:46,549 --> 01:14:48,417
-[Servo] There, you see.
-[Joel and Crow] Hey!

1885
01:14:48,484 --> 01:14:49,652
He did it again.

1886
01:14:49,719 --> 01:14:52,555
[Joel] So they're just incorporating
the fact that they're just close friends.

1887
01:14:54,323 --> 01:14:55,992
[all] He's everywhere.
He's everywhere.

1888
01:15:01,731 --> 01:15:03,866
[Joel] Little, honey,
did I say something?

1889
01:15:05,668 --> 01:15:08,170
[Crow] I don't think Little Man
is cut out for a rampage.

1890
01:15:08,237 --> 01:15:11,440
[♪♪♪]

1891
01:15:14,944 --> 01:15:17,747
[Servo] Oh, wait,
the little man. Ow, owie! Ow.

1892
01:15:21,851 --> 01:15:24,153
[Joel] Now, what were
you so mad about?

1893
01:15:25,755 --> 01:15:28,090
[Crow] Should I taunt him?
Nah, he's dead.

1894
01:15:31,394 --> 01:15:33,963
[Servo] Oh, oh.
Hi, just cleaning up down here.

1895
01:15:34,030 --> 01:15:36,098
Look what I found. Does he belong to you?

1896
01:15:40,903 --> 01:15:43,105
[Joel] Oh, good,
you killed Little Man.

1897
01:15:44,106 --> 01:15:45,674
[Crow] Am I in time for happy hour?

1898
01:15:45,741 --> 01:15:47,843
I could really go
for some mozzarella sticks.

1899
01:15:51,947 --> 01:15:53,516
[Servo] Uh, you're standing
on his head, dear.

1900
01:15:53,582 --> 01:15:54,617
[Crow] Ew.

1901
01:15:55,618 --> 01:15:56,952
How'd it happen?

1902
01:15:57,987 --> 01:15:59,388
Jake tried to kill him.

1903
01:16:00,556 --> 01:16:01,624
It was self-defense.

1904
01:16:01,690 --> 01:16:04,126
And thus the first L.A. cop was born.

1905
01:16:05,127 --> 01:16:06,195
That right?

1906
01:16:07,196 --> 01:16:08,330
You might call it that.

1907
01:16:15,738 --> 01:16:17,273
[Joel] She's quiet today.

1908
01:16:19,341 --> 01:16:20,276
[Servo] Oh goodness, yes.

1909
01:16:20,342 --> 01:16:21,644
I always come here on Saturday

1910
01:16:21,710 --> 01:16:24,113
{\an8}because they have that
really nice breakfast burrito.

1911
01:16:24,180 --> 01:16:25,114
You know, you take eggs and...

1912
01:16:25,181 --> 01:16:26,248
What time is it?

1913
01:16:26,315 --> 01:16:28,551
It's still 7:15,
like the last time you asked me.

1914
01:16:28,617 --> 01:16:30,453
Take it easy, Gideon.

1915
01:16:30,519 --> 01:16:32,254
Did you see Cane Miro this morning?

1916
01:16:32,321 --> 01:16:33,889
Not yet.

1917
01:16:33,956 --> 01:16:35,624
[Crow] You're hard to talk to.

1918
01:16:35,691 --> 01:16:37,126
You feel up to meeting the mail at eight?

1919
01:16:37,193 --> 01:16:38,794
[Joel] No, but thanks for asking.

1920
01:16:39,361 --> 01:16:40,362
It's my duty.

1921
01:16:41,363 --> 01:16:42,765
I failed it once.

1922
01:16:44,366 --> 01:16:45,835
I won't again.

1923
01:16:45,901 --> 01:16:47,670
[Servo] Ah, you probably will,
but let's go.

1924
01:16:47,736 --> 01:16:48,838
Wait until he gets here.

1925
01:16:48,904 --> 01:16:50,773
No sense muffing this
with a miss at long range.

1926
01:16:50,840 --> 01:16:52,007
You didn't pay for this. It's your shot.

1927
01:16:52,074 --> 01:16:54,443
[Crow] Hey, she got
her horse reupholstered.

1928
01:16:57,947 --> 01:16:59,615
-Hi, folks!
-[Servo] Hey, guard.

1929
01:16:59,682 --> 01:17:01,450
What brings you way out here so early?

1930
01:17:01,517 --> 01:17:02,518
Have you got the railroad letter?

1931
01:17:02,585 --> 01:17:04,420
Right here, safe and sound.

1932
01:17:04,487 --> 01:17:06,155
That's nice to know.

1933
01:17:06,222 --> 01:17:07,256
Hand it over.

1934
01:17:07,323 --> 01:17:08,858
[Servo] You gotta sign for it.

1935
01:17:09,792 --> 01:17:12,328
[Joel] There's postage due
on that letter, ma'am.

1936
01:17:12,394 --> 01:17:14,430
[Crow] Which one of you
gets the<i> Starlog?</i>

1937
01:17:15,231 --> 01:17:16,699
Now get out of here.

1938
01:17:17,900 --> 01:17:19,201
[Joel] You're welcome.

1939
01:17:21,570 --> 01:17:23,906
[Servo] Oh, there's a switch.
Someone's shooting a postal worker.

1940
01:17:25,541 --> 01:17:27,877
[Joel] Mom wants to stay with us,
so see for yourself.

1941
01:17:27,943 --> 01:17:28,878
Not coming.

1942
01:17:29,512 --> 01:17:32,081
[Joel] Yeah, but Peg
sends her regards.

1943
01:17:32,148 --> 01:17:34,150
They're going to build
the line through Rockdale.

1944
01:17:35,017 --> 01:17:37,953
-That's a shame.
-Is that all you can say?

1945
01:17:38,020 --> 01:17:40,189
-It's a darn shame.
-[Servo] That's better.

1946
01:17:40,789 --> 01:17:42,691
You ready to help me knock over the town?

1947
01:17:43,626 --> 01:17:44,894
I've got two bullets,

1948
01:17:44,960 --> 01:17:48,230
one for Rose, and one for Captain Polk.

1949
01:17:49,465 --> 01:17:52,001
[Crow] Hey, she's littering.
There's a fine for that.

1950
01:17:54,003 --> 01:17:55,704
Nine o'clock.

1951
01:17:55,771 --> 01:17:57,873
It's never been this late before.

1952
01:17:57,940 --> 01:17:59,575
Something's happened to him.

1953
01:18:00,242 --> 01:18:01,877
Think I'd better ride out and meet him.

1954
01:18:01,944 --> 01:18:03,646
No, you'd better stay here.

1955
01:18:03,712 --> 01:18:04,980
You go on, Rose.

1956
01:18:05,047 --> 01:18:06,849
Gideon and I can take care of ourselves.

1957
01:18:06,916 --> 01:18:08,684
[Joel] Speak for yourself, honey.

1958
01:18:08,751 --> 01:18:09,885
[Servo] Dun-dun-dun! Oh!

1959
01:18:09,952 --> 01:18:11,820
<i>♪ Oklahoma, where the w-- ♪</i>

1960
01:18:11,887 --> 01:18:13,722
-Oh, forget it.
-Move away, folks.

1961
01:18:13,789 --> 01:18:15,891
Might be some shootin' around here.

1962
01:18:15,958 --> 01:18:18,827
Nobody on the street except
Fred, Mayor Polk, and me.

1963
01:18:18,894 --> 01:18:21,430
[Joel] Well, that's pretty much
the whole town, pretty much.

1964
01:18:23,299 --> 01:18:26,368
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

1965
01:18:26,869 --> 01:18:28,971
[Servo] ♪ Who'll catch McCain
<i>He's got.-- ♪</i>

1966
01:18:29,038 --> 01:18:30,940
-[Servo] Oh, never mind.
-[dog barking]

1967
01:18:34,510 --> 01:18:36,111
[dramatic trumpet flourish]

1968
01:18:36,178 --> 01:18:37,947
[Servo imitating trumpet flourish]

1969
01:18:38,013 --> 01:18:40,816
[Crow] Tell Sergeant O'Rourke
it's the Harkawis.

1970
01:18:40,916 --> 01:18:43,619
[Joel] Well, look, they have
a Fotomat over there.

1971
01:18:43,686 --> 01:18:46,088
[Crow] Yeah.
And it's saying, "Oh, no!"

1972
01:18:46,155 --> 01:18:48,090
[Joel and Servo chuckle]

1973
01:18:48,157 --> 01:18:49,592
[Servo] Army man.

1974
01:18:49,692 --> 01:18:52,061
-Joshua!
-[Joel] Light show.

1975
01:18:52,127 --> 01:18:54,096
Looks like he means to hold us up.

1976
01:18:54,163 --> 01:18:55,898
You'll have to get him.

1977
01:18:55,965 --> 01:18:57,433
You'll have to pay for it.

1978
01:18:57,499 --> 01:18:59,768
I gave you 3,000 to take care
of the law in Oracle.

1979
01:18:59,835 --> 01:19:00,769
He's part of it.

1980
01:19:00,836 --> 01:19:01,770
So you did.

1981
01:19:01,837 --> 01:19:03,572
I should've listened to the fine print.

1982
01:19:03,639 --> 01:19:04,807
Take the other side of the road.

1983
01:19:06,108 --> 01:19:07,176
That's far enough!

1984
01:19:08,043 --> 01:19:09,278
[Joel] Guess not.

1985
01:19:10,779 --> 01:19:12,214
They shot Joshua!

1986
01:19:12,281 --> 01:19:16,819
[Servo] ♪ They didn't shoot the sheriff
But they did shoot the deputy ♪

1987
01:19:18,287 --> 01:19:20,122
Haven't even got a gun
to protect myself with.

1988
01:19:20,189 --> 01:19:21,690
[Crow as Star Trek's Scottie]
I'm losing power, Captain.

1989
01:19:21,757 --> 01:19:22,891
I'll find you one.

1990
01:19:22,958 --> 01:19:25,894
[Joel] And put on another pair
of pants, for God's sakes.

1991
01:19:25,961 --> 01:19:27,396
Where are you going?

1992
01:19:27,463 --> 01:19:29,064
After something to shoot with.

1993
01:19:29,131 --> 01:19:30,532
You better stay here.

1994
01:19:31,567 --> 01:19:33,535
That won't do you any good.

1995
01:19:33,602 --> 01:19:36,005
Gideon asked for a gun
and I aim to find one for him.

1996
01:19:36,071 --> 01:19:38,474
[Crow] But there's
a ten-day waiting period.

1997
01:19:38,540 --> 01:19:40,042
I'm afraid it's too late.

1998
01:19:46,782 --> 01:19:49,418
[Servo] Hey, could you tell us
where the Red Dog Saloon is?

1999
01:19:49,485 --> 01:19:50,719
-Where's the marshal?
-She rode out of town.

2000
01:19:52,921 --> 01:19:53,822
What's the matter?

2001
01:19:54,590 --> 01:19:56,692
Thought I saw an old friend.

2002
01:19:56,759 --> 01:19:57,693
[Joel] Oops, got to pee.

2003
01:19:57,760 --> 01:19:59,361
You haven't got time for the mayor.

2004
01:19:59,428 --> 01:20:01,196
I've waited 15 years.

2005
01:20:01,263 --> 01:20:03,098
This is as good a time
as any to settle it.

2006
01:20:03,165 --> 01:20:05,734
[Servo whispers]
Plop, plop, plop, plop, plop, plop, plop.

2007
01:20:06,602 --> 01:20:07,736
He's after you!

2008
01:20:09,672 --> 01:20:10,773
Get out of sight!

2009
01:20:11,640 --> 01:20:13,375
[Crow] Whoa, guess
he's not the hero anymore.

2010
01:20:16,145 --> 01:20:17,313
Felicity!

2011
01:20:17,379 --> 01:20:19,081
[Servo] There's a beef roast in the...
[groaning]

2012
01:20:19,148 --> 01:20:21,383
-[Crow] Yes, where?
-Don't be afraid for me.

2013
01:20:22,184 --> 01:20:24,219
Just get yourself away from here.

2014
01:20:24,286 --> 01:20:25,554
[Joel] Retire to Florida.

2015
01:20:25,621 --> 01:20:30,492
You don't have to be brave
just for some no-account killer.

2016
01:20:30,559 --> 01:20:33,228
[Crow] Got you out
the school marm. Sorry.

2017
01:20:36,065 --> 01:20:37,466
[Servo] You were supposed
to get me a gun.

2018
01:20:37,533 --> 01:20:39,234
Oh, great. What's next?

2019
01:20:39,301 --> 01:20:40,369
Uh. Oh.

2020
01:20:41,804 --> 01:20:44,373
[Joel] Dri-- I mean, wait a sec.

2021
01:20:46,875 --> 01:20:49,611
[Crow] Could we maybe settle this
with a game of Scrabble?

2022
01:20:52,348 --> 01:20:53,749
[Joel] American Gothic; solo.

2023
01:20:56,418 --> 01:20:58,320
[Crow] ♪ Da-ner-da-ner-ner!
<i>Got chores! ♪</i>

2024
01:20:58,387 --> 01:21:00,622
[Servo] ♪ Da-doot-da-doot-doot!
<i>The hell? ♪</i>

2025
01:21:04,393 --> 01:21:06,061
[Joel] I'm sorry, you look too stupid.

2026
01:21:06,128 --> 01:21:07,129
I can't shoot you.

2027
01:21:09,765 --> 01:21:12,067
[Crow] Bad idea. Fork thing didn't work.

2028
01:21:15,604 --> 01:21:18,073
[Servo] Oh, hi, honey.
Gee, I've had a very productive day.

2029
01:21:18,741 --> 01:21:20,776
Alright, you've taken care
of your personal pleasures.

2030
01:21:20,843 --> 01:21:22,378
Rose will be here any minute.

2031
01:21:22,444 --> 01:21:23,412
It's your show.

2032
01:21:23,479 --> 01:21:26,315
-[Servo] Hi.
-Ride to the alley by your hotel and wait.

2033
01:21:26,382 --> 01:21:28,384
I'll be in the Land Office
across the street.

2034
01:21:28,450 --> 01:21:29,318
[Crow] Who's this guy?

2035
01:21:29,385 --> 01:21:31,553
You drag these bodies up
to the street by the alley.

2036
01:21:32,121 --> 01:21:33,856
When Rose gets here, keep her talking.

2037
01:21:33,922 --> 01:21:35,724
If you give us away, I'll kill you.

2038
01:21:35,791 --> 01:21:36,892
Anything you say.

2039
01:21:36,959 --> 01:21:38,560
Get moving!

2040
01:21:38,627 --> 01:21:40,896
-You plan fast.
-I always have.

2041
01:21:40,963 --> 01:21:42,364
I'll signal you when to take her.

2042
01:21:42,431 --> 01:21:44,433
[Joel] You seem
really crabby today.

2043
01:21:48,070 --> 01:21:50,606
[Crow] Oh, you leave town
and your work piles up.

2044
01:21:52,207 --> 01:21:54,376
[Joel] Yeah, I don't like being
the sheriff anymore.

2045
01:21:59,681 --> 01:22:00,649
[Crow] Should be two Ls.

2046
01:22:01,049 --> 01:22:03,318
[Joel] Well, one's OK.

2047
01:22:03,719 --> 01:22:05,053
[Servo] Oh, hi, everyone's dead.

2048
01:22:05,120 --> 01:22:06,455
They got the mayor, and his wife too.

2049
01:22:08,857 --> 01:22:10,859
Killers rode out of town.

2050
01:22:11,260 --> 01:22:13,462
-[Crow] Nooner, come on.
-[Servo whispers] No, not now.

2051
01:22:13,562 --> 01:22:15,097
Did you see who they were?

2052
01:22:15,164 --> 01:22:16,598
No, I didn't get a good look.

2053
01:22:18,333 --> 01:22:19,568
[Crow] Nooner, you know...

2054
01:22:19,635 --> 01:22:20,936
[Servo whispers]
No. What do you mean?

2055
01:22:21,003 --> 01:22:23,105
Are you sure it wasn't
Cane Miro and Erica?

2056
01:22:23,172 --> 01:22:24,807
Oh, I'm positive it wasn't.

2057
01:22:26,508 --> 01:22:28,644
-[Crow] Come on.
-[Servo whispers] There's no time.

2058
01:22:32,314 --> 01:22:34,149
[Crow] Guess
there's no nooner then.

2059
01:22:37,719 --> 01:22:38,687
It's all right.

2060
01:22:40,556 --> 01:22:42,324
That's why I couldn't talk.

2061
01:22:42,391 --> 01:22:44,893
-Who am I after?
-Cane Miro.

2062
01:22:45,928 --> 01:22:47,062
Thanks.

2063
01:22:47,162 --> 01:22:49,031
[Joel] Remind me to kill you later.

2064
01:22:49,097 --> 01:22:51,900
[♪♪♪]

2065
01:22:52,634 --> 01:22:58,640
[Servo] Robby, Steve,
Donny, Uncle Charlie...

2066
01:23:03,712 --> 01:23:04,880
[Joel] Hey, there's
Jeep tracks on that hill.

2067
01:23:04,947 --> 01:23:06,448
[Crow] Yeah, I thought so.

2068
01:23:08,784 --> 01:23:10,118
[Servo] This film
makes<i> Dirty Dingus Magee</i>

2069
01:23:10,185 --> 01:23:11,787
look like a John Ford film.

2070
01:23:11,854 --> 01:23:12,988
[Crow laughs] I can't...

2071
01:23:14,923 --> 01:23:16,859
[Crow] The 12 days and the Baja 500.

2072
01:23:18,427 --> 01:23:20,662
-[Joel] Are they circling each other?
-[Servo] I think so.

2073
01:23:23,999 --> 01:23:26,201
[Servo] Now he's in Ireland.
What's going on?

2074
01:23:29,471 --> 01:23:30,772
[Crow] From Vermont to New Mexico.

2075
01:23:33,675 --> 01:23:36,144
[Joel] Power-assisted antilock hoofs.

2076
01:23:39,748 --> 01:23:41,917
[Crow] Well, I'll just
follow these Jeep tracks.

2077
01:23:49,358 --> 01:23:52,027
[Servo] Guys, that's a baobab tree.

2078
01:23:52,094 --> 01:23:53,428
Now they're in the Serengeti.

2079
01:23:58,867 --> 01:24:01,637
[Joel] Man, I wish there was
a Pump 'n' Lunch around here.

2080
01:24:07,109 --> 01:24:09,545
[Crow] Tonight, on a very special
<i>Guns of Will Sonnett...</i>

2081
01:24:09,611 --> 01:24:11,747
[Servo with old man voice]
Son? Dagnabbit.

2082
01:24:13,282 --> 01:24:14,483
[gun cocks]

2083
01:24:16,618 --> 01:24:19,688
[Servo] Ha! I like how the horse is
so affected by the gunfire.

2084
01:24:21,023 --> 01:24:23,158
Nice day for shooting rabbits.

2085
01:24:23,258 --> 01:24:26,328
[Crow] Actually it's better
when it's a little overcast.

2086
01:24:26,395 --> 01:24:28,230
That any way to talk to an old friend?

2087
01:24:28,330 --> 01:24:29,298
Don't be a fool, Cane.

2088
01:24:29,364 --> 01:24:30,699
I'm out here to kill you.

2089
01:24:30,799 --> 01:24:32,501
I wouldn't do that to you.

2090
01:24:32,601 --> 01:24:33,869
I know you've been missing on purpose,

2091
01:24:33,936 --> 01:24:35,537
but it won't do you any good.

2092
01:24:35,604 --> 01:24:37,406
[Joel] You know, they should start
dating other people.

2093
01:24:37,472 --> 01:24:38,774
-[Servo] Mm-hmm.
-[Crow] Yep, or shooting 'em.

2094
01:24:38,840 --> 01:24:41,109
You haven't been doing so well yourself.

2095
01:24:41,209 --> 01:24:44,079
[Servo] I think maybe they should read
<i>You Just Don't Understand.</i>

2096
01:24:45,380 --> 01:24:47,549
[Crow] Back in those days, when
you had relationship problems,

2097
01:24:47,616 --> 01:24:49,618
you really had relationship problems.

2098
01:24:50,652 --> 01:24:52,287
[Servo] That hurts.

2099
01:24:52,354 --> 01:24:53,388
Rose?

2100
01:24:53,989 --> 01:24:55,023
Yes?

2101
01:24:55,624 --> 01:24:56,792
In case I don't see you again,

2102
01:24:56,858 --> 01:24:58,894
there's something I'd like to ask you.

2103
01:24:58,994 --> 01:25:00,062
What is it?

2104
01:25:00,462 --> 01:25:01,396
Do you...?

2105
01:25:01,463 --> 01:25:03,131
[Joel] What's Fred MacMurray like?

2106
01:25:03,198 --> 01:25:05,200
Is it a two-way thing?

2107
01:25:05,267 --> 01:25:06,802
[Joel] He just popped that
out of his shoulder.

2108
01:25:08,737 --> 01:25:09,838
It's a two-way thing.

2109
01:25:13,175 --> 01:25:14,743
[Servo] Oh, I guess
it's kind of one-way now.

2110
01:25:20,015 --> 01:25:21,383
[Crow] This is kind of like
<i>Ride the High Country,</i>

2111
01:25:21,483 --> 01:25:23,251
except it's not very cool.

2112
01:25:31,560 --> 01:25:33,128
[Joel] You shoot like a girl.

2113
01:25:34,429 --> 01:25:35,297
Rose?

2114
01:25:35,364 --> 01:25:37,065
[Servo] Hey, you don't have eight
or nine pounds of plasma

2115
01:25:37,132 --> 01:25:38,367
on you, do you?

2116
01:25:41,136 --> 01:25:42,337
Rose?

2117
01:25:42,437 --> 01:25:44,539
[Crow] Come on, pick up.
I know you're there.

2118
01:25:48,977 --> 01:25:51,313
-[Joel] Oh, right in the hat.
-[Servo] Ouch.

2119
01:25:57,653 --> 01:26:00,188
[Servo] Uh, now I'm going
to have to make new friends.

2120
01:26:01,823 --> 01:26:03,458
[Crow] She'll have to start
a new town now.

2121
01:26:03,525 --> 01:26:04,493
[Servo laughs] Yeah.

2122
01:26:11,333 --> 01:26:14,970
{\an8}[Joel] What did you mean
by that two-way thing?

2123
01:26:18,073 --> 01:26:19,875
{\an8}[Servo] God, the paperwork!

2124
01:26:22,177 --> 01:26:24,379
[Crow] Well, now she's
the sheriff of herself.

2125
01:26:24,446 --> 01:26:27,215
[Joel] Yeah, well, at least
the horses are cheap now.

2126
01:26:30,419 --> 01:26:31,353
You found him.

2127
01:26:31,420 --> 01:26:33,121
[Servo] Well, we canceled Crazy Days.

2128
01:26:33,188 --> 01:26:35,791
Yeah. Here.

2129
01:26:36,458 --> 01:26:39,428
[Crow] Look, before we say anything else,
are you setting me up here?

2130
01:26:39,494 --> 01:26:41,363
By the twisted tree near Boot Hill.

2131
01:26:41,430 --> 01:26:43,098
[Joel] Oh, I love that place.

2132
01:26:44,700 --> 01:26:47,302
Jimmy, I'm leaving Oracle.
I don't want to see this place again.

2133
01:26:48,370 --> 01:26:49,738
When the new marshal gets here...

2134
01:26:51,273 --> 01:26:52,174
give him this.

2135
01:26:52,240 --> 01:26:53,875
[Servo] You don't need a marshal.
There's no people.

2136
01:26:53,942 --> 01:26:56,011
My things are packed.
They're in the marshal's office.

2137
01:26:56,078 --> 01:26:59,081
-[Joel] Give him all my bras too.
-Send 'em to Santa Fe for me?

2138
01:26:59,147 --> 01:27:00,716
Be glad to, Mrs. Hood.

2139
01:27:01,917 --> 01:27:04,519
-Thanks.
-[Crow] By the way, who are you?

2140
01:27:04,586 --> 01:27:06,588
[Servo] And don't set up
the new marshal.

2141
01:27:08,056 --> 01:27:09,191
[Servo in feminine voice]
Well, goodbye, everybody.

2142
01:27:09,257 --> 01:27:10,358
[Crow] We're all dead.

2143
01:27:10,425 --> 01:27:11,960
[Servo] Oh, that's right.

2144
01:27:13,128 --> 01:27:14,830
[Servo making hoofbeat noises]

2145
01:27:16,665 --> 01:27:17,999
[Joel] Hi, I'm here to kill you.

2146
01:27:19,968 --> 01:27:22,838
'Scuse me, ma'am.
My name is Sam Bass.

2147
01:27:22,904 --> 01:27:25,107
Can you tell me where I might
find the marshal's office?

2148
01:27:27,042 --> 01:27:27,976
<i>It's right down there.</i>

2149
01:27:28,043 --> 01:27:29,444
-[Crow] Third body on the left.
-Thanks, ma'am.

2150
01:27:30,178 --> 01:27:32,547
<i>Looks like a nice,</i>
<i>quiet little town you've got here.</i>

2151
01:27:32,614 --> 01:27:33,882
[Servo] Dead quiet.

2152
01:27:33,949 --> 01:27:34,816
<i>Yeah.</i>

2153
01:27:35,984 --> 01:27:37,052
<i>Yeah, it is.</i>

2154
01:27:37,119 --> 01:27:38,653
[Joel] Except for all the bodies.

2155
01:27:38,720 --> 01:27:41,790
[♪♪♪]

2156
01:27:43,625 --> 01:27:46,394
[Servo]<i> ♪ All that glitters is gold ♪</i>

2157
01:27:46,695 --> 01:27:47,763
[Servo humming]

2158
01:27:47,963 --> 01:27:49,631
[Servo] Hey, lady, you forget
to tell me where the--

2159
01:27:49,698 --> 01:27:50,866
Oh, my God!

2160
01:27:50,932 --> 01:27:52,567
[Servo screams]

2161
01:27:53,301 --> 01:27:54,503
-[Joel laughs]
-[Crow] Oh, my.

2162
01:27:54,569 --> 01:27:57,038
[Joel] Oh, boy!
That was turd, wasn't it?

2163
01:28:09,885 --> 01:28:12,587
You know, Roger Corman can make
almost anything seem dismal,

2164
01:28:12,654 --> 01:28:16,391
but still, the 1870s
had to be a pretty foul decade, eh?

2165
01:28:16,458 --> 01:28:18,460
Well, I barely remember the 1870s,

2166
01:28:18,527 --> 01:28:20,662
but I was around for the 1970s,

2167
01:28:20,729 --> 01:28:23,198
and you're right,
it was a pretty foul decade.

2168
01:28:23,265 --> 01:28:26,134
Cool. Well, did you wear chaps
and cowboy hats and stuff?

2169
01:28:26,201 --> 01:28:28,403
Uh, no, but I knew people who did.

2170
01:28:28,470 --> 01:28:29,838
Were the James gang still around?

2171
01:28:29,905 --> 01:28:32,641
Oh, no, Joel Walsh broke up
and started Barnstorm.

2172
01:28:32,707 --> 01:28:36,244
Oh, hey, did you ever rope cattle
or bust broncos and stuff?

2173
01:28:36,311 --> 01:28:38,914
No, but I rolled
my Charger a few times.

2174
01:28:38,980 --> 01:28:40,115
[bots] Wow.

2175
01:28:40,182 --> 01:28:42,284
Well, let's read some letters, huh?
Where are they?

2176
01:28:42,350 --> 01:28:43,718
Uh... Yeah, they're down there.

2177
01:28:43,785 --> 01:28:46,454
-Oh.
-Yup, fresh, crispy letters.

2178
01:28:46,521 --> 01:28:49,724
Hey, they are fresh and crispy. Ew!

2179
01:28:49,791 --> 01:28:52,594
-Yeah, we deep fried 'em.
-Why?

2180
01:28:52,661 --> 01:28:54,930
Uh, I'm not sure I understand
the question, Joel.

2181
01:28:54,996 --> 01:28:58,733
Uh, never mind, let's just
blot out some of this grease,

2182
01:28:58,800 --> 01:29:02,437
break off some of this admittedly
delicious looking crust--

2183
01:29:02,504 --> 01:29:04,306
Ooh, caution, filling is hot.

2184
01:29:04,372 --> 01:29:06,308
-[Crow] Yup. Be careful.
-OK...

2185
01:29:06,374 --> 01:29:10,245
And about how many weeks' worth
of letters did you fry anyway?

2186
01:29:10,312 --> 01:29:13,081
Well, like four mail bags full,
whatever that is.

2187
01:29:13,148 --> 01:29:16,351
Yup. We had a lot of frying medium
and a lot of letters.

2188
01:29:16,418 --> 01:29:19,354
Well, honeys, don't deep fry
any more letters, OK?

2189
01:29:19,421 --> 01:29:20,589
-Yeah, OK.
-Yeah, OK.

2190
01:29:20,655 --> 01:29:22,591
OK, this letter is from France.

2191
01:29:22,657 --> 01:29:24,392
-French.
-Ooh la la.

2192
01:29:24,459 --> 01:29:26,494
{\an8}And put that on still storage French.

2193
01:29:26,561 --> 01:29:32,567
{\an8}And that's from Mike Murph,
Amy, Dan, Nancy, Jeff and Marie.

2194
01:29:32,901 --> 01:29:35,770
And they write, "Dear fellows,
our club is made up of members

2195
01:29:35,837 --> 01:29:37,973
from Nice, Monaco, and Menton.

2196
01:29:38,039 --> 01:29:40,342
And we meet regularly
to scarf down Mexican food

2197
01:29:40,408 --> 01:29:42,210
and watch the latest 10 tapes

2198
01:29:42,277 --> 01:29:46,481
sent over by our supplier
in Southern California."

2199
01:29:46,548 --> 01:29:47,549
[Servo] Wink, wink.

2200
01:29:47,616 --> 01:29:49,317
"So far, our club
is exclusively American,

2201
01:29:49,384 --> 01:29:51,219
as the British folks
we've tried to recruit

2202
01:29:51,286 --> 01:29:54,089
just haven't gotten
all really excited.

2203
01:29:54,155 --> 01:29:56,358
But hey, what can
you expect from the people

2204
01:29:56,424 --> 01:29:57,926
who gave us<i> Benny Hill?"</i>

2205
01:29:57,993 --> 01:29:59,661
Hey, they gave us Monty Python too.

2206
01:29:59,728 --> 01:30:01,162
[all] Yeah.

2207
01:30:01,229 --> 01:30:03,565
But, there is that Benny Hill thing.

2208
01:30:03,632 --> 01:30:06,268
Yup. There it sits.

2209
01:30:06,334 --> 01:30:08,103
Well, what do you think, sirs?

2210
01:30:08,536 --> 01:30:10,272
[Crow humming "Benny Hill Theme"]

2211
01:30:10,505 --> 01:30:11,773
-[Servo] Don't!
-[Crow] Blah.

2212
01:30:13,575 --> 01:30:14,709
[gasps]

2213
01:30:14,776 --> 01:30:16,311
Wow, it worked.

2214
01:30:16,378 --> 01:30:18,580
I blew Frank's head up.

2215
01:30:18,647 --> 01:30:20,882
Well, remind me
to snap on a new one, Joel.

2216
01:30:20,949 --> 01:30:22,617
Until next time...

2217
01:30:23,118 --> 01:30:25,053
[eerie music playing]

2218
01:30:28,723 --> 01:30:31,760
[theme music playing]

2219
01:31:30,185 --> 01:31:31,786
{\an8}Don't bother going back to town!

2220
01:31:31,853 --> 01:31:33,855
{\an8}I want you out of this state tonight!

2221
01:31:33,922 --> 01:31:35,123
{\an8}What about our clothes?

